s.com/29926/1689275404-ill-book-list.png?fit=clip&h=162&w=282\",\"width\":282,\"height\":158,\"aspectRatio\":1.782234957020057,\"alt\":null,\"title\":null,\"base64\":\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\",\"bgColor\":\"#cfa222\"}}},{\"title\":\"Oscar-Nominated Films Based on Books: 2026\",\"description\":\"Read before you watch these Oscar-nominated films!\",\"id\":\"VP5jXOZYRwiDqxIm8pluMw\",\"url\":\"https://search.worldcat.org/lists/2ad8833f-a690-4d26-991e-4b7f5c30d65c\",\"image\":{\"responsiveImage\":{\"srcSet\":\"https://www.datocms-assets.com/29926/1779387441-218000-worldcat_lists_imagery_oscar-nominated.png?dpr=0.25&fit=clip&h=162&w=282 70w,https://www.datocms-assets.com/29926/1779387441-218000-worldcat_lists_imagery_oscar-nominated.png?dpr=0.5&fit=clip&h=162&w=282 141w,https://www.datocms-assets.com/29926/1779387441-218000-worldcat_lists_imagery_oscar-nominated.png?dpr=0.75&fit=clip&h=162&w=282 211w,https://www.datocms-assets.com/29926/1779387441-218000-worldcat_lists_imagery_oscar-nominated.png?fit=clip&h=162&w=282 282w,https://www.datocms-assets.com/29926/1779387441-218000-worldcat_lists_imagery_oscar-nominated.png?dpr=1.5&fit=clip&h=162&w=282 423w,https://www.datocms-assets.com/29926/1779387441-218000-worldcat_lists_imagery_oscar-nominated.png?dpr=2&fit=clip&h=162&w=282 564w\",\"webpSrcSet\":\"https://www.datocms-assets.com/29926/1779387441-218000-worldcat_lists_imagery_oscar-nominated.png?dpr=0.25&fit=clip&fm=webp&h=162&w=282 70w,https://www.datocms-assets.com/29926/1779387441-218000-worldcat_lists_imagery_oscar-nominated.png?dpr=0.5&fit=clip&fm=webp&h=162&w=282 141w,https://www.datocms-assets.com/29926/1779387441-218000-worldcat_lists_imagery_oscar-nominated.png?dpr=0.75&fit=clip&fm=webp&h=162&w=282 211w,https://www.datocms-assets.com/29926/1779387441-218000-worldcat_lists_imagery_oscar-nominated.png?fit=clip&fm=webp&h=162&w=282 282w,https://www.datocms-assets.com/29926/1779387441-218000-worldcat_lists_imagery_oscar-nominated.png?dpr=1.5&fit=clip&fm=webp&h=162&w=282 423w,https://www.datocms-assets.com/29926/1779387441-218000-worldcat_lists_imagery_oscar-nominated.png?dpr=2&fit=clip&fm=webp&h=162&w=282 564w\",\"sizes\":\"(max-width: 282px) 100vw, 282px\",\"src\":\"https://www.datocms-assets.com/29926/1779387441-218000-worldcat_lists_imagery_oscar-nominated.png?fit=clip&h=162&w=282\",\"width\":282,\"height\":158,\"aspectRatio\":1.782234957020057,\"alt\":null,\"title\":null,\"base64\":\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\",\"bgColor\":\"#ecb579\"}}},{\"title\":\"National Book Awards 2025\",\"description\":\"This list includes the longlist, finalists and one winner of each of the following award categories: fiction, nonfiction, poetry, translated literature, and young people's literature.\",\"id\":\"185894806\",\"url\":\"https://search.worldcat.org/lists/14f2f31e-a7d5-47bc-a965-50af909deae1\",\"image\":{\"responsiveImage\":{\"srcSet\":\"https://www.datocms-assets.com/29926/1779387229-218000-worldcat_lists_imagery_national-book-awards.png?dpr=0.25&fit=clip&h=162&w=282 70w,https://www.datocms-assets.com/29926/1779387229-218000-worldcat_lists_imagery_national-book-awards.png?dpr=0.5&fit=clip&h=162&w=282 141w,https://www.datocms-assets.com/29926/1779387229-218000-worldcat_lists_imagery_national-book-awards.png?dpr=0.75&fit=clip&h=162&w=282 211w,https://www.datocms-assets.com/29926/1779387229-218000-worldcat_lists_imagery_national-book-awards.png?fit=clip&h=162&w=282 282w,https://www.datocms-assets.com/29926/1779387229-218000-worldcat_lists_imagery_national-book-awards.png?dpr=1.5&fit=clip&h=162&w=282 423w,https://www.datocms-assets.com/29926/1779387229-218000-worldcat_lists_imagery_national-book-awards.png?dpr=2&fit=clip&h=162&w=282 564w\",\"webpSrcSet\":\"https://www.datocms-assets.com/29926/1779387229-218000-worldcat_lists_imagery_national-book-awards.png?dpr=0.25&fit=clip&fm=webp&h=162&w=282 70w,https://www.datocms-assets.com/29926/1779387229-218000-worldcat_lists_imagery_national-book-awards.png?dpr=0.5&fit=clip&fm=webp&h=162&w=282 141w,https://www.datocms-assets.com/29926/1779387229-218000-worldcat_lists_imagery_national-book-awards.png?dpr=0.75&fit=clip&fm=webp&h=162&w=282 211w,https://www.datocms-assets.com/29926/1779387229-218000-worldcat_lists_imagery_national-book-awards.png?fit=clip&fm=webp&h=162&w=282 282w,https://www.datocms-assets.com/29926/1779387229-218000-worldcat_lists_imagery_national-book-awards.png?dpr=1.5&fit=clip&fm=webp&h=162&w=282 423w,https://www.datocms-assets.com/29926/1779387229-218000-worldcat_lists_imagery_national-book-awards.png?dpr=2&fit=clip&fm=webp&h=162&w=282 564w\",\"sizes\":\"(max-width: 282px) 100vw, 282px\",\"src\":\"https://www.datocms-assets.com/29926/1779387229-218000-worldcat_lists_imagery_national-book-awards.png?fit=clip&h=162&w=282\",\"width\":282,\"height\":158,\"aspectRatio\":1.782234957020057,\"alt\":null,\"title\":null,\"base64\":\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\",\"bgColor\":\"#d89136\"}}},{\"title\":\"The Booker Prize: 2025\",\"description\":\"View the longlist for the Booker Prize 2025.\",\"id\":\"B1kanhKUTpCKXCctKCQmTQ\",\"url\":\"https://search.worldcat.org/lists/e1674e2f-68d8-4c94-900f-64641f61b994\",\"image\":{\"responsiveImage\":{\"srcSet\":\"https://www.datocms-assets.com/29926/1779387324-218000-worldcat_lists_imagery_the-booker-prize.png?dpr=0.25&fit=clip&h=162&w=282 70w,https://www.datocms-assets.com/29926/1779387324-218000-worldcat_lists_imagery_the-booker-prize.png?dpr=0.5&fit=clip&h=162&w=282 141w,https://www.datocms-assets.com/29926/1779387324-218000-worldcat_lists_imagery_the-booker-prize.png?dpr=0.75&fit=clip&h=162&w=282 211w,https://www.datocms-assets.com/29926/1779387324-218000-worldcat_lists_imagery_the-booker-prize.png?fit=clip&h=162&w=282 282w,https://www.datocms-assets.com/29926/1779387324-218000-worldcat_lists_imagery_the-booker-prize.png?dpr=1.5&fit=clip&h=162&w=282 423w,https://www.datocms-assets.com/29926/1779387324-218000-worldcat_lists_imagery_the-booker-prize.png?dpr=2&fit=clip&h=162&w=282 564w\",\"webpSrcSet\":\"https://www.datocms-assets.com/29926/1779387324-218000-worldcat_lists_imagery_the-booker-prize.png?dpr=0.25&fit=clip&fm=webp&h=162&w=282 70w,https://www.datocms-assets.com/29926/1779387324-218000-worldcat_lists_imagery_the-booker-prize.png?dpr=0.5&fit=clip&fm=webp&h=162&w=282 141w,https://www.datocms-assets.com/29926/1779387324-218000-worldcat_lists_imagery_the-booker-prize.png?dpr=0.75&fit=clip&fm=webp&h=162&w=282 211w,https://www.datocms-assets.com/29926/1779387324-218000-worldcat_lists_imagery_the-booker-prize.png?fit=clip&fm=webp&h=162&w=282 282w,https://www.datocms-assets.com/29926/1779387324-218000-worldcat_lists_imagery_the-booker-prize.png?dpr=1.5&fit=clip&fm=webp&h=162&w=282 423w,https://www.datocms-assets.com/29926/1779387324-218000-worldcat_lists_imagery_the-booker-prize.png?dpr=2&fit=clip&fm=webp&h=162&w=282 564w\",\"sizes\":\"(max-width: 282px) 100vw, 282px\",\"src\":\"https://www.datocms-assets.com/29926/1779387324-218000-worldcat_lists_imagery_the-booker-prize.png?fit=clip&h=162&w=282\",\"width\":282,\"height\":158,\"aspectRatio\":1.782234957020057,\"alt\":null,\"title\":null,\"base64\":\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\",\"bgColor\":\"#2f9eb4\"}}}],\"featuredUserListHeading\":\"Popular WorldCat.org user lists\",\"featuredUserListMoreInfoLink\":[]},\"fetchedStaffListData\":[{\"listMetadata\":{\"id\":\"40adb58c-db5f-4f2d-9de3-5163b8651f9a\",\"displayOwner\":{\"nameVisible\":true},\"listName\":\"Global Accessibility Awareness Day 2026\",\"description\":\"Global Accessibility Awareness Day (GAAD) is observed annually on the third Thursday in May. Check out these resources to learn how to improve digital products, web content, and apps, making them accessible to all.\",\"listType\":\"worldcat-org\",\"public\":true,\"countOfItems\":21,\"countOfFollowers\":8,\"created\":\"2026-05-12T17:46:11.432Z\",\"modified\":\"2026-05-20T13:58:35.250Z\",\"modifiedBy\":\"SaraP\",\"ownerRegistryId\":268401},\"items\":[{\"id\":11181613916,\"itemType\":\"BibRecordSummary\",\"title\":\"Accessibility metadata: A journey to understanding and implementation\",\"creator\":\"Claire Holloway\",\"publicationDate\":\"2026\",\"itemRecord\":{\"citationUrl\":\"https://dx.doi.org/10.1177/18758789261435328\",\"contributors\":[{\"firstName\":{\"text\":\"Claire\"},\"isPrimary\":true,\"secondName\":{\"text\":\"Holloway\"}},{\"firstName\":{\"text\":\"Emily\"},\"isPrimary\":false,\"secondName\":{\"text\":\"Gilreath\"}},{\"firstName\":{\"text\":\"Morris\"},\"isPrimary\":false,\"secondName\":{\"text\":\"Levy\"}},{\"firstName\":{\"text\":\"Timothy\"},\"isPrimary\":false,\"secondName\":{\"text\":\"Savage\"}}],\"creator\":\"Claire Holloway\",\"date\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.1177/18758789261435328\",\"generalFormat\":\"ArtChap\",\"isBookReview\":false,\"isNewsArticle\":false,\"machineReadableDate\":\"2026\",\"oclcNumber\":\"11181613916\",\"peerReviewed\":\"Y\",\"source\":[{\"publicationInformation\":\"Sage UK: London, England, SAGE Publications\",\"relatedParts\":[\"v46 n1-2 (202605): 28-40\"],\"sourceIssn\":\"0167-5265\",\"sourceTitle\":\"Information Services and Use\"},{\"firstPages\":[\"28\"],\"issueDates\":[\"202605\"],\"issueDatesNormalized\":[\"202605\"],\"issues\":[\"1-2\"],\"pageRanges\":[\"28-40\"],\"volumes\":[\"46\"]}],\"sourceIssns\":[\"0167-5265\",\"1875-8789\"],\"specificFormat\":\"Artcl\",\"subjectsText\":[\"European Accessibility Act\",\"metadata\",\"OCLC\",\"ONIX\",\"MARC records\",\"W3C EPUB Accessibility\",\"information accessibility\",\"standards\"],\"summariesText\":[\"This paper is based upon the OCLC presentation at the February 2025 NISO Plus conference. It describes the organization’s journey to research compliance to the European Accessibility Act (EAA). It focuses on the three major complications that shaped their approach: the tension between internal and external metadata sources, the challenge of translating between different metadata formats, and the balance between controlled vocabularies and descriptive flexibility. Their investigation began with three questions: What metadata does the EAA actually require? How will this information flow through existing supply chains? And where should accessibility data be recorded in MARC records to best serve users. OCLC’s journey unearthed a complex landscape involving questions of trust between publishers and libraries, the limitations of existing standards, and the fundamental tension between textual description and systematic discovery. They hope that sharing these experiences will help other organizations navigate similar challenges more efficiently, while contributing to the broader efforts to standardize accessibility metadata that benefit the entire community of libraries, publishers, and content aggregators\"],\"title\":\"Accessibility metadata: A journey to understanding and implementation\",\"titleInfo\":{\"text\":\"Accessibility metadata: A journey to understanding and implementation\"}}},{\"id\":1228511736,\"itemType\":\"BibRecordSummary\",\"title\":\"Building For Everyone\",\"creator\":\"Annie Jean-Baptiste\",\"publicationDate\":\"2020\",\"itemRecord\":{\"catalogingLanguage\":\"eng\",\"citationUrl\":\"https://ezproxy.torontopubliclibrary.ca/login?url=https://learning.oreilly.com/library/view/-/9781119646228/\",\"contributors\":[{\"firstName\":{\"text\":\"Annie\"},\"isPrimary\":true,\"relatorCodes\":[\"aut\"],\"secondName\":{\"text\":\"Jean-Baptiste\"}},{\"isPrimary\":false,\"nonPersonName\":{\"text\":\"O'Reilly for Higher Education (Firm)\"},\"relatorCodes\":[\"dst\"]},{\"isPrimary\":false,\"nonPersonName\":{\"text\":\"Safari, an O'Reilly Media Company\"}},{\"isPrimary\":false,\"nonPersonName\":{\"text\":\"John Wiley & Sons\"},\"relatorCodes\":[\"pbl\"]}],\"creator\":\"Annie Jean-Baptiste\",\"date\":\"2020\",\"edition\":\"1st edition\",\"generalFormat\":\"Book\",\"isBookReview\":false,\"isNewsArticle\":false,\"isbns\":[\"9781119646228\",\"1119646227\"],\"language\":\"eng\",\"machineReadableDate\":\"2020\",\"oclcNumber\":\"1228511736\",\"peerReviewed\":\"N\",\"publicationPlace\":\"[Place of publication not identified]\",\"publisher\":\"Wiley\",\"specificFormat\":\"Digital\",\"subjectsText\":[\"Product design\",\"Universal design\",\"Conception de produit\",\"Conception universelle\"],\"summariesText\":[\"Diversity and Inclusion to build better products from the front lines at Google Establishing diverse and inclusive organizations is an economic imperative for every industry. Any business that isn't reaching a diverse market is missing out on enormous revenue potential and the opportunity to build products that suit their users' core needs. The economic \\\"why\\\" has been firmly established, but what about the \\\"how?\\\" How can business leaders adapt to our ever-more-diverse world by capturing market share AND building more inclusive products for people of color, women and other underrepresented groups? The Product Inclusion Team at Google has developed strategies to do just that and Building For Everyone is the practical guide to following in their footsteps. This book makes publicly available for the first time the same inclusive design process used at Google to create user-centric award-winning and profitable products. Author and Head of Product Inclusion Annie Jean-Baptiste outlines what those practices look like in industries beyond tech with fascinating case studies. Readers will learn the key strategies and step-by-step processes for inclusive product design that limits risk and increases profitability. Discover the questions you should be asking about diversity and inclusion in your products for marketers, user researchers, product managers and more. Understand the research the Product Inclusion team drove to back up their practices Learn the \\\"ABCs of Product Inclusion\\\" to build inclusion into your organization's culture Leverage the product inclusion suite of tools to get your organization building more inclusively and identifying new opportunities. Read case studies to see how product inclusion works across industries and learn what doesn't work. Building For Everyone will show you how to infuse your business processes with inclusive design. You'll learn best practices for inclusion in product design, marketing, management, leadership and beyond, straight from the innovative Google Product Inclusion team\"],\"title\":\"Building For Everyone\",\"titleInfo\":{\"text\":\"Building For Everyone\"}}},{\"id\":1523834436,\"itemType\":\"BibRecordSummary\",\"title\":\"Agile accessibility handbook : a practical guide to accessible software development at scale\",\"creator\":\"Dylan Barrell\",\"publicationDate\":\"2020\",\"itemRecord\":{\"catalogingLanguage\":\"eng\",\"contributors\":[{\"firstName\":{\"text\":\"Dylan\"},\"isPrimary\":true,\"secondName\":{\"text\":\"Barrell\"}}],\"creator\":\"Dylan Barrell\",\"date\":\"2020\",\"generalFormat\":\"Book\",\"isBookReview\":false,\"isNewsArticle\":false,\"isbns\":[\"9781645434771\",\"164543477X\"],\"language\":\"eng\",\"machineReadableDate\":\"2020\",\"oclcNumber\":\"1523834436\",\"peerReviewed\":\"N\",\"publicationPlace\":\"Herndon, VA\",\"publisher\":\"Amplify Publishing\",\"specificFormat\":\"PrintBook\",\"subjectsText\":[\"People with disabilities Web applications\",\"Accessible Web sites for people with disabilities\",\"Assistive computer technology\",\"Sites Web accessibles aux personnes handicapées\",\"Technologie informatique adaptée\",\"handbooks\",\"Handbooks and manuals\",\"Guides et manuels\"],\"summariesText\":[\"\\\"It is estimated that one in five people has a disability; if you do the math, that's a huge, addressable market that is often overlooked. Digital Accessibility practitioners tap into this market by making digital documents as well as web and mobile apps accessible to everyone. However, many enterprises struggle to create, maintain, and scale their digital accessibility efforts. Agile Accessibility Handbook outlines the steps organizations can take to capture this market, avoid risk, maintain agility, and close the accessibility gap. Using the information provided within this handbook, accessibility subject matter experts, development team members, and executives in charge of setting priorities can together learn how to build successful accessibility experiences for everyone.\\\"--amazon.com\"],\"title\":\"Agile accessibility handbook : a practical guide to accessible software development at scale\",\"titleInfo\":{\"text\":\"Agile accessibility handbook : a practical guide to accessible software development at scale\"}}},{\"id\":1025413063,\"itemType\":\"BibRecordSummary\",\"title\":\"Mismatch : how inclusion shapes design\",\"creator\":\"Kat Holmes\",\"publicationDate\":\"2018\",\"itemRecord\":{\"catalogingLanguage\":\"eng\",\"contributors\":[{\"firstName\":{\"text\":\"Kat\"},\"isPrimary\":true,\"relatorCodes\":[\"aut\"],\"secondName\":{\"text\":\"Holmes\"}}],\"creator\":\"Kat Holmes\",\"date\":\"2018\",\"generalFormat\":\"Book\",\"isBookReview\":false,\"isNewsArticle\":false,\"isbns\":[\"9780262038881\",\"0262038889\",\"9780262539487\",\"0262539489\"],\"language\":\"eng\",\"machineReadableDate\":\"2018\",\"mergedOclcNumbers\":[\"1029652413\",\"1029788823\",\"1029849282\",\"1493275828\"],\"oclcNumber\":\"1025413063\",\"peerReviewed\":\"N\",\"publicationPlace\":\"Cambridge, Massachusetts\",\"publisher\":\"The MIT Press\",\"series\":\"Simplicity (Cambridge, Mass.)\",\"specificFormat\":\"PrintBook\",\"subjectsText\":[\"Design Anthropological aspects\",\"Social integration\",\"Marginality, Social\",\"Social Integration\",\"Design Aspect anthropologique\",\"Intégration sociale\"],\"summariesText\":[\"\\\"Sometimes designed objects reject their users: a computer mouse that doesn't work for left-handed people, for example, or a touchscreen payment system that only works for people who read English phrases, have 20/20 vision, and use a credit card. Something as simple as color choices can render a product unusable for millions. These mismatches are the building blocks of exclusion. In Mismatch, Kat Holmes describes how design can lead to exclusion, and how design can also remedy exclusion. Inclusive design methods--designing objects with rather than for excluded users--can create elegant solutions that work well and benefit all. Holmes tells stories of pioneers of inclusive design, many of whom were drawn to work on inclusion because of their own experiences of exclusion. A gamer and designer who depends on voice recognition shows Holmes his 'Wall of Exclusion, ' which displays dozens of game controllers that require two hands to operate; an architect shares her firsthand knowledge of how design can fail communities, gleaned from growing up in Detroit's housing projects; an astronomer who began to lose her eyesight adapts a technique called 'sonification' so she can 'listen' to the stars. Designing for inclusion is not a feel-good sideline. Holmes shows how inclusion can be a source of innovation and growth, especially for digital technologies. It can be a catalyst for creativity and a boost for the bottom line as a customer base expands. And each time we remedy a mismatched interaction, we create an opportunity for more people to contribute to society in meaningful ways.\\\"--Publisher's description\"],\"title\":\"Mismatch : how inclusion shapes design\",\"titleInfo\":{\"text\":\"Mismatch : how inclusion shapes design\"}}},{\"id\":1569680396,\"itemType\":\"BibRecordSummary\",\"title\":\"Accessible UX research\",\"creator\":\"Michele A. Williams\",\"publicationDate\":\"2025\",\"itemRecord\":{\"accessibilityNote\":[{\"displayConstant\":\"Accessibility features\",\"material\":{\"text\":\"EBSCOhost\"},\"summary\":{\"text\":\"\\\"EBSCO evaluates our products based on the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) and the related Section 508 and EN 301 549 regulations in the US and EU. Most EBSCO products are substantially conformant with WCAG 2.2 level AA.\\\" Source: https://connect.ebsco.com/s/article/EBSCO-VPATs?language=en_US. Last accessed April 22, 2025.\"}}],\"catalogingLanguage\":\"eng\",\"citationUrl\":\"https://search.ebscohost.com/login.aspx?direct=true&scope=site&db=nlebk&db=nlabk&AN=4407870\",\"contributors\":[{\"firstName\":{\"text\":\"Michele A.\"},\"isPrimary\":true,\"secondName\":{\"text\":\"Williams\"}}],\"creator\":\"Michele A. Williams\",\"date\":\"2025\",\"generalFormat\":\"Book\",\"isBookReview\":false,\"isNewsArticle\":false,\"isbns\":[\"9783910835030\",\"3910835031\",\"9783910835047\",\"391083504X\"],\"language\":\"eng\",\"machineReadableDate\":\"2025\",\"mergedOclcNumbers\":[\"1569333684\"],\"oclcNumber\":\"1569680396\",\"peerReviewed\":\"N\",\"publicationPlace\":\"[Place of publication not identified]\",\"publisher\":\"Smashing Magazine\",\"specificFormat\":\"Digital\",\"subjectsText\":[\"User interfaces (Computer systems)\",\"Interfaces utilisateurs (Informatique)\"],\"title\":\"Accessible UX research\",\"titleInfo\":{\"text\":\"Accessible UX research\"}}},{\"id\":1475275030,\"itemType\":\"BibRecordSummary\",\"title\":\"Accessible communications : create impact, avoid missteps and build trust\",\"creator\":\"Lisa Riemers\",\"publicationDate\":\"2026\",\"itemRecord\":{\"catalogingLanguage\":\"eng\",\"contributors\":[{\"firstName\":{\"text\":\"Lisa\"},\"isPrimary\":true,\"relatorCodes\":[\"aut\"],\"secondName\":{\"text\":\"Riemers\"}},{\"firstName\":{\"text\":\"Matisse\"},\"isPrimary\":false,\"relatorCodes\":[\"aut\"],\"secondName\":{\"text\":\"Hamel-Nelis\"}}],\"creator\":\"Lisa Riemers\",\"date\":\"2026\",\"generalFormat\":\"Book\",\"incorrectIsbns\":[\"9781398621855\"],\"isBookReview\":false,\"isNewsArticle\":false,\"isbns\":[\"9781398621848\",\"1398621846\",\"9781398621862\",\"1398621862\"],\"language\":\"eng\",\"machineReadableDate\":\"2026\",\"mergedOclcNumbers\":[\"1475276359\"],\"oclcNumber\":\"1475275030\",\"peerReviewed\":\"N\",\"publicationPlace\":\"London\",\"publisher\":\"Kogan Page\",\"specificFormat\":\"PrintBook\",\"subjectsText\":[\"Business communication\",\"Public relations\",\"Social responsibility of business\",\"Communication dans l'entreprise\",\"Entreprises Responsabilité sociale\",\"Relations publiques\",\"public relations\"],\"summariesText\":[\"\\\"Overlooking accessibility can be expensive, but integrating it from the start amplifies reach and saves money in the long run. Accessible communications expand audiences, boost sales, protect reputations and ensure everyone can access information without exclusion. This practical and easy-to-follow guide ensures mid-level communicators feel confident in creating truly accessible communications across various formats, from emails and documents to videos and social. With the emphasis on practical content examples that professionals encounter daily and a holistic approach, this book will become the ultimate companion to anyone looking to communicate information effectively. Whether that's internal communications for colleagues or external messages for customers, suppliers, shareholders or other stakeholders. Written by two leading communications consultants who provide in-depth coverage of evolving legislation in the area and a forward-looking approach that goes beyond compliance and looks towards clarity and inclusivity, this book equips communicators to develop communications that build business reputation and consumer trust. With real-world examples, this book ensures that all communications are inclusive and effective\\\"-- Provided by publisher\"],\"title\":\"Accessible communications : create impact, avoid missteps and build trust\",\"titleInfo\":{\"text\":\"Accessible communications : create impact, avoid missteps and build trust\"}}},{\"id\":1545067346,\"itemType\":\"BibRecordSummary\",\"title\":\"Digital accessibility ethics : disability inclusion in all things tech\",\"creator\":\"Lainey Feingold\",\"publicationDate\":\"2026\",\"itemRecord\":{\"catalogingLanguage\":\"eng\",\"contributors\":[{\"firstName\":{\"text\":\"Lainey\"},\"isPrimary\":false,\"relatorCodes\":[\"edt\"],\"secondName\":{\"text\":\"Feingold\"}},{\"firstName\":{\"text\":\"Reginé M.\"},\"isPrimary\":false,\"relatorCodes\":[\"edt\"],\"secondName\":{\"text\":\"Gilbert\"}},{\"firstName\":{\"text\":\"Chancey\"},\"isPrimary\":false,\"relatorCodes\":[\"edt\"],\"secondName\":{\"text\":\"Fleet\"}}],\"creator\":\"Lainey Feingold\",\"date\":\"2026\",\"edition\":\"First edition\",\"generalFormat\":\"Book\",\"incorrectIsbns\":[\"9781003616702\",\"9781040604762\",\"9781040571583\"],\"isBookReview\":false,\"isNewsArticle\":false,\"isbns\":[\"9781041018698\",\"104101869X\",\"9781041018681\",\"1041018681\"],\"language\":\"eng\",\"machineReadableDate\":\"2026\",\"mergedOclcNumbers\":[\"1545052283\",\"1593505474\"],\"oclcNumber\":\"1545067346\",\"peerReviewed\":\"N\",\"publicationPlace\":\"Boca Raton\",\"publisher\":\"CRC Press, Taylor & Francis Group\",\"specificFormat\":\"PrintBook\",\"subjectsText\":[\"Computers and people with disabilities\",\"Accessible Web sites for people with disabilities\",\"Digital divide\",\"People with disabilities Services for\",\"Computer software Development Moral and ethical aspects\",\"Information technology Moral and ethical aspects\",\"Ordinateurs et personnes handicapées\",\"Sites Web accessibles aux personnes handicapées\",\"Fossé numérique\",\"Personnes handicapées Services\",\"Computer software Development\"],\"summariesText\":[\"\\\"Digital Accessibility Ethics is a practical guide with an urgent goal: to help end tech exclusion of 1.3 billion people across the world with disabilities. The book introduces the first Digital Accessibility Ethics Framework - an action-oriented, three-part tool designed to influence, change, and disrupt patterns of exclusion with values, actions, and questions. 39 authors from 10 countries and one commonwealth, the majority of whom are disabled, apply this Framework across technologies, sectors, and countries. The editors and authors - with over 600 years of combined accessibility and disability advocacy experience -- aim to build a world that recognizes disabled people's right to fully participate in every facet of digital life. And to offer organizations an ethics lens to help eliminate the financial, legal, privacy, safety, and other risks and harms of disability exclusion. Through stories, recommendations, strategies, and other guidance, the book looks at a wide range of topics through an ethics lens: from gaming and smart cities to hackathons, procurement, and cybersecurity. From accessibility practitioner burnout, to robots, artificial intelligence, aerospace, design, healthcare, open source, emergency preparedness, legal ethics, publishing and much more. This book is for technologists, educators, students, marketers, policy makers and everyone who has ever posted on social media or sent an email. It encourages us to stop and ask ourselves: who are we excluding by our actions? Who are we harming, what are we risking, by our decisions? As the world grows more digital, as AI is marketed everywhere, and as the number of people with disabilities continues to grow, there has never been a more urgent time to expose, explore, and act at the intersection of ethics, disability, and digital accessibility. Digital Accessibility Ethics offers a roadmap to show us the way\\\"-- Provided by publisher\"],\"title\":\"Digital accessibility ethics : disability inclusion in all things tech\",\"titleInfo\":{\"text\":\"Digital accessibility ethics : disability inclusion in all things tech\"}}},{\"id\":1372499580,\"itemType\":\"BibRecordSummary\",\"title\":\"Guide to digital accessibility : policies, practices, and professional development\",\"creator\":\"Rae Mancilla\",\"publicationDate\":\"2023\",\"itemRecord\":{\"catalogingLanguage\":\"eng\",\"contributors\":[{\"firstName\":{\"text\":\"Rae\"},\"isPrimary\":false,\"relatorCodes\":[\"edt\"],\"secondName\":{\"text\":\"Mancilla\"}},{\"firstName\":{\"text\":\"Barbara A.\"},\"isPrimary\":false,\"relatorCodes\":[\"edt\"],\"secondName\":{\"text\":\"Frey\"}}],\"creator\":\"Rae Mancilla\",\"date\":\"2023\",\"edition\":\"First edition\",\"generalFormat\":\"Book\",\"incorrectIsbns\":[\"9781642674545\",\"9781642674552\"],\"isBookReview\":false,\"isNewsArticle\":false,\"isbns\":[\"9781642674521\",\"1642674524\",\"9781642674538\",\"1642674532\",\"1642674524\",\"9781642674521\"],\"language\":\"eng\",\"machineReadableDate\":\"2023\",\"mergedOclcNumbers\":[\"1352795713\",\"1352795895\"],\"oclcNumber\":\"1372499580\",\"peerReviewed\":\"N\",\"publicationPlace\":\"Sterling, Virginia\",\"publisher\":\"Stylus\",\"specificFormat\":\"PrintBook\",\"subjectsText\":[\"Internet in higher education\",\"Web-based instruction\",\"Internet dans l'enseignement supérieur\",\"Internet en la enseñanza superior\",\"Enseñanza en línea\"],\"summariesText\":[\"\\\"Written for practitioners by practitioners, this book addresses vital compliance issues and maps a range of proven practices that will create and enrich online learning experiences that are accessible and usable by all learners\\\"-- Provided by publisher\"],\"title\":\"Guide to digital accessibility : policies, practices, and professional development\",\"titleInfo\":{\"text\":\"Guide to digital accessibility : policies, practices, and professional development\"}}},{\"id\":1528630819,\"itemType\":\"BibRecordSummary\",\"title\":\"Inclusive design for accessibility : a practical guide to digital accessibility, UX, and inclusive web & app design\",\"creator\":\"Dale Cruse\",\"publicationDate\":\"2025\",\"itemRecord\":{\"accessibilityNote\":[{\"displayConstant\":\"Accessibility features\",\"material\":{\"text\":\"EBSCOhost\"},\"summary\":{\"text\":\"\\\"EBSCO evaluates our products based on the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) and the related Section 508 and EN 301 549 regulations in the US and EU. Most EBSCO products are substantially conformant with WCAG 2.2 level AA.\\\" Source: https://connect.ebsco.com/s/article/EBSCO-VPATs?language=en_US. Last accessed April 22, 2025\"}}],\"catalogingLanguage\":\"eng\",\"citationUrl\":\"https://search.ebscohost.com/login.aspx?direct=true&scope=site&db=nlebk&db=nlabk&AN=4270552\",\"contributors\":[{\"firstName\":{\"text\":\"Dale\"},\"isPrimary\":true,\"relatorCodes\":[\"aut\"],\"secondName\":{\"text\":\"Cruse\"}},{\"firstName\":{\"text\":\"Denis\"},\"isPrimary\":false,\"relatorCodes\":[\"aut\"],\"secondName\":{\"text\":\"Boudreau\"}}],\"creator\":\"Dale Cruse\",\"date\":\"2025\",\"generalFormat\":\"Book\",\"isBookReview\":false,\"isNewsArticle\":false,\"isbns\":[\"1835888232\",\"9781835888230\",\"1835888224\",\"9781835888223\"],\"language\":\"eng\",\"machineReadableDate\":\"2025\",\"oclcNumber\":\"1528630819\",\"peerReviewed\":\"N\",\"publicationPlace\":\"Birmingham\",\"publisher\":\"Packt Publishing\",\"specificFormat\":\"Digital\",\"subjectsText\":[\"Computer software Human factors\",\"Computers and people with disabilities\",\"Software engineering Social aspects\",\"Logiciels Facteurs humains\",\"Ordinateurs et personnes handicapées\",\"Génie logiciel Aspect social\",\"Software engineering\"],\"summariesText\":[\"\\\"In \\\"\\\"Inclusive Design for Accessibility,\\\"\\\" you'll learn how to create digital experiences that truly empower all users, regardless of their abilities. This book covers the principles of inclusive design, practical strategies, and real-world examples, helping you integrate accessibility into every step of your design and development process. What this Book will help me do Master the core principles of inclusive design to cater to a diverse audience. Develop accessible interfaces for various platforms including web, mobile, and emerging technologies. Conduct effective user research to better understand diverse needs and integrate accessibility insights. Leverage AI to improve and automate accessibility features in digital products. Foster an organizational culture that prioritizes accessibility and inclusive design. Author(s) Dale Cruse and Denis Boudreau are highly respected experts in the field of digital accessibility and inclusive design. Dale has extensive experience in user experience and interface design, while Denis is a recognized leader and consultant in accessibility advocacy and education. Together, they bring valuable expertise and hands-on strategies to help readers tackle real-world accessibility challenges. Who is it for? This book is ideal for digital professionals, including designers, developers, UX practitioners, and product managers, who aim to create inclusive digital products. It's suited for beginners to advanced practitioners eager to understand and implement accessibility. Additionally, it serves business leaders looking to foster accessibility in organizational culture and fulfill legal compliance.\\\"\"],\"title\":\"Inclusive design for accessibility : a practical guide to digital accessibility, UX, and inclusive web & app design\",\"titleInfo\":{\"text\":\"Inclusive design for accessibility : a practical guide to digital accessibility, UX, and inclusive web & app design\"}}},{\"id\":1131698037,\"itemType\":\"BibRecordSummary\",\"title\":\"Inclusive components : accessible web interfaces, piece by piece\",\"creator\":\"Heydon Pickering\",\"publicationDate\":\"2019\",\"itemRecord\":{\"catalogingLanguage\":\"eng\",\"contributors\":[{\"firstName\":{\"text\":\"Heydon\"},\"isPrimary\":true,\"relatorCodes\":[\"aut\"],\"secondName\":{\"text\":\"Pickering\"}}],\"creator\":\"Heydon Pickering\",\"date\":\"2019\",\"generalFormat\":\"Book\",\"isBookReview\":false,\"isNewsArticle\":false,\"isbns\":[\"9783945749821\",\"3945749824\"],\"language\":\"eng\",\"machineReadableDate\":\"2019\",\"oclcNumber\":\"1131698037\",\"peerReviewed\":\"N\",\"publicationPlace\":\"Freiburg, Germany\",\"publisher\":\"Smashing Magazine AG\",\"specificFormat\":\"PrintBook\",\"subjectsText\":[\"Web sites Design\",\"Accessible Web sites for people with disabilities\",\"Computers and people with disabilities\",\"Sites Web Conception\",\"Sites Web accessibles aux personnes handicapées\",\"Ordinateurs et personnes handicapées\"],\"summariesText\":[\"\\\"In his brand-new book Inclusive Components, Heydon Pickering explores more accessible and robust solutions for the UI patterns we author, plug in, and use every day. Written for front-end developers who want to detect and address potential accessibility issues in their components, you'll not only learn to see common web UI patterns through the lens of inclusion and adopt an inclusive mindset but practical code samples and working demos help you make a change right away.\\\"-- From Smashing Magazine website\"],\"title\":\"Inclusive components : accessible web interfaces, piece by piece\",\"titleInfo\":{\"text\":\"Inclusive components : accessible web interfaces, piece by piece\"}}},{\"id\":1494975796,\"itemType\":\"BibRecordSummary\",\"title\":\"Dark and Silent Office : A Digital Accessibility Guidebook for Inclusive Communication in the Workplace\",\"creator\":\"Stephanie Warlick\",\"publicationDate\":\"2024\",\"itemRecord\":{\"catalogingLanguage\":\"eng\",\"contributors\":[{\"firstName\":{\"text\":\"Stephanie\"},\"isPrimary\":true,\"relatorCodes\":[\"aut\"],\"secondName\":{\"text\":\"Warlick\"}},{\"firstName\":{\"text\":\"Glenda\"},\"isPrimary\":false,\"secondName\":{\"text\":\"Sims\"}}],\"creator\":\"Stephanie Warlick\",\"date\":\"2024\",\"generalFormat\":\"Book\",\"isBookReview\":false,\"isNewsArticle\":false,\"isbns\":[\"9798989821808\"],\"language\":\"eng\",\"machineReadableDate\":\"2024\",\"oclcNumber\":\"1494975796\",\"peerReviewed\":\"N\",\"publicationPlace\":\"[Place of publication not identified]\",\"publisher\":\"5FT View Consulting, LLC\",\"specificFormat\":\"PrintBook\",\"subjectsText\":[\"Accessible Web sites for people with disabilities Planning\",\"Computers and people with disabilities\",\"Technology and people with disabilities\",\"Assistive computer technology\",\"Sites Web accessibles aux personnes handicapées Planification\",\"Ordinateurs et personnes handicapées\",\"Technologie informatique adaptée\"],\"summariesText\":[\"Ask anyone and they would agree that technology is a necessary component of the workplace. But have you ever relied on technology and it failed -- just before your deadline? Think about having that experience all day, every day while attempting to meet your daily work objectives. There are approximately 37.5 million adults in the US with trouble hearing and another 50.18 million adults with some degree of vision loss. The fight for equity in the workplace has very much focused on gender and race, and while these steps are completely necessary, visually-disabled and hearing-disabled individuals are a minority group that is significantly overlooked. Jenny sat in a meeting where the manager was detailing the quarterly financial review. As they discussed the colors of charts and diagrams, Jenny, being colorblind, couldn't keep up. She left the meeting exhausted and deflated. Mark was typing away on his computer when the team leader informed the office about an important update. If it hadn't been for his colleague advising him, Mark, being deaf, would have missed out on this information. Nobody intentionally excludes the visually and hearing impaired. But that's not enough in the year 2024 where the benefits of inclusivity have been demonstrated time and time again. But there is a huge gap between wanting an inclusive workplace and actually achieving it. It's a gap that you find yourself standing in right now! The workplace is buzzing in a digital era and overall, technology is closing so many gaps across the industries. At the same time, it's sadly making the gap bigger for those with sight and hearing difficulties\"],\"title\":\"Dark and Silent Office : A Digital Accessibility Guidebook for Inclusive Communication in the Workplace\",\"titleInfo\":{\"text\":\"Dark and Silent Office : A Digital Accessibility Guidebook for Inclusive Communication in the Workplace\"}}},{\"id\":1518507037,\"itemType\":\"BibRecordSummary\",\"title\":\"The accessibility operations guidebook : to making accessibility work more sustainable\",\"creator\":\"Devon Persing\",\"publicationDate\":\"2025\",\"itemRecord\":{\"catalogingLanguage\":\"eng\",\"contributors\":[{\"firstName\":{\"text\":\"Devon\"},\"isPrimary\":true,\"relatorCodes\":[\"aut\"],\"secondName\":{\"text\":\"Persing\"}}],\"creator\":\"Devon Persing\",\"date\":\"2025\",\"edition\":\"First edition\",\"generalFormat\":\"Book\",\"isBookReview\":false,\"isNewsArticle\":false,\"isbns\":[\"9798307802304\"],\"language\":\"eng\",\"machineReadableDate\":\"2025\",\"oclcNumber\":\"1518507037\",\"peerReviewed\":\"N\",\"publicationPlace\":\"[S.l.]\",\"publisher\":\"ADMIT HUB REF SERVICE PR\",\"specificFormat\":\"PrintBook\",\"subjectsText\":[\"Digital accessibility\",\"Guidebook\",\"Assistive computer technology\",\"Technologie informatique adaptée\"],\"summariesText\":[\"\\\"The accessibility field has a burnout problem. People get into this work to make accessible products and services. But, they often find themselves doing a lot of other work - program management, legal compliance, and constant, constant advocacy - instead. This isn't usually what people sign up for, and it leads directly to burnout. / This book seeks to help break that cycle. It's not about accessibility work itself, but about building digital programs that are more sustainable, intersectional, and data-driven. / The first part of the book is a crash course in social science. It introduces theories about organizational psychology, community, education, information literacy, work burnout, disability, and intersectionality. / The second part is a strategy guide. It takes the theories from the first part and applies them to building an accessibility practice that better fits your needs and those of your organization. It's about using data and systems thinking to help you focus on the hard work of growing community, centering disability and disabled people, and enabling accessibility instead of policing it\"],\"title\":\"The accessibility operations guidebook : to making accessibility work more sustainable\",\"titleInfo\":{\"text\":\"The accessibility operations guidebook : to making accessibility work more sustainable\"}}},{\"id\":871042774,\"itemType\":\"BibRecordSummary\",\"title\":\"A web for everyone : designing accessible user experiences\",\"creator\":\"Sarah Horton\",\"publicationDate\":\"2013\",\"itemRecord\":{\"catalogingLanguage\":\"eng\",\"contributors\":[{\"contributorNotes\":{\"date\":[\"1962-\"]},\"firstName\":{\"text\":\"Sarah\"},\"isPrimary\":true,\"relatorCodes\":[\"aut\"],\"secondName\":{\"text\":\"Horton\"}},{\"firstName\":{\"text\":\"Whitney\"},\"isPrimary\":false,\"relatorCodes\":[\"aut\"],\"secondName\":{\"text\":\"Quesenbery\"}}],\"creator\":\"Sarah Horton\",\"date\":\"2013\",\"generalFormat\":\"Book\",\"isBookReview\":false,\"isNewsArticle\":false,\"isbns\":[\"9781933820972\",\"1933820977\"],\"language\":\"eng\",\"machineReadableDate\":\"2013\",\"oclcNumber\":\"871042774\",\"peerReviewed\":\"N\",\"publicationPlace\":\"Brooklyn, New York\",\"publisher\":\"Rosenfeld Media\",\"specificFormat\":\"PrintBook\",\"subjectsText\":[\"Accessible Web sites for people with disabilities\",\"Web site development\",\"Internet\",\"Human-computer interaction\",\"Sites Web accessibles aux personnes handicapées\",\"Sites Web Développement\"],\"summariesText\":[\"A Web for Everyone will help you make your site accessible without sacrificing design or innovation. Rooted in universal design principles, this book provides solutions: practical advice and examples of how to create sites that everyone can use\"],\"title\":\"A web for everyone : designing accessible user experiences\",\"titleInfo\":{\"text\":\"A web for everyone : designing accessible user experiences\"}}},{\"id\":1578999555,\"itemType\":\"BibRecordSummary\",\"title\":\"Digital outcasts : moving technology forward without leaving people behind\",\"creator\":\"Kel Smith\",\"publicationDate\":\"2026\",\"itemRecord\":{\"catalogingLanguage\":\"eng\",\"contributors\":[{\"firstName\":{\"text\":\"Kel\"},\"isPrimary\":true,\"relatorCodes\":[\"aut\"],\"secondName\":{\"text\":\"Smith\"}}],\"creator\":\"Kel Smith\",\"date\":\"2026\",\"edition\":\"Second edition\",\"generalFormat\":\"Book\",\"incorrectIsbns\":[\"9780443336782\"],\"isBookReview\":false,\"isNewsArticle\":false,\"isbns\":[\"9780443336775\",\"0443336776\"],\"language\":\"eng\",\"machineReadableDate\":\"2026\",\"oclcNumber\":\"1578999555\",\"peerReviewed\":\"N\",\"publicationPlace\":\"Amsterdam\",\"publisher\":\"Morgan Kaufmann Publisher, an imprint of Elsevier\",\"specificFormat\":\"PrintBook\",\"subjectsText\":[\"Assistive computer technology\",\"Computers and people with disabilities\",\"Technologie informatique adaptée\",\"Ordinateurs et personnes handicapées\"],\"summariesText\":[\"\\\"Comprehensively explores inclusive design in human-computer interaction. The book examines the real-life experiences of people with disabilities as they navigate systemic barriers in employment, education, healthcare, and social connectivity. This new edition covers the intersectionality of disability with other forms of economic and political discrimination, uncovering how biases related to race, gender, and ability are reflected in language models and AI algorithms. With digital access a foundational element of human existence, the consequences of exclusion are far-reaching and increasingly urgent. Citing case studies in law, creative arts, and social science, this updated edition also examines the historical and emergent impact people with disabilities have on culture and industry. Digital Outcasts emphases that disability has long served as a powerful catalyst for design innovation, driving transformational benefit for consumers of all abilities and backgrounds. Taking into account new legal and technological perspectives, this revision stands as an update on the progress we have made—and how far we have yet to go.\\\"--Publisher's website\"],\"title\":\"Digital outcasts : moving technology forward without leaving people behind\",\"titleInfo\":{\"text\":\"Digital outcasts : moving technology forward without leaving people behind\"}}},{\"id\":1548304168,\"itemType\":\"BibRecordSummary\",\"title\":\"Inclusive design for a digital world : designing with accessibility in mind\",\"creator\":\"Regine M. Gilbert\",\"publicationDate\":\"2025\",\"itemRecord\":{\"accessibilityContent\":[{\"access\":{\"material\":{\"text\":\"PDF\"},\"textual\":{\"text\":\"All non-decorative content supports reading without sight\"}},\"content\":\"primary\"},{\"access\":{\"material\":{\"text\":\"PDF\"},\"textual\":{\"text\":\"Next / Previous structural navigation\"}},\"content\":\"primary\"},{\"access\":{\"material\":{\"text\":\"PDF\"},\"textual\":{\"text\":\"PDF/UA-1\"}},\"content\":\"primary\"},{\"access\":{\"material\":{\"text\":\"PDF\"},\"textual\":{\"text\":\"Short alternative textual descriptions\"}},\"content\":\"primary\"},{\"access\":{\"material\":{\"text\":\"PDF\"},\"textual\":{\"text\":\"Single logical reading order\"}},\"content\":\"primary\"},{\"access\":{\"material\":{\"text\":\"PDF\"},\"textual\":{\"text\":\"Table of contents navigation\"}},\"content\":\"primary\"},{\"access\":{\"material\":{\"text\":\"PDF\"},\"textual\":{\"text\":\"Use of color is not sole means of conveying information\"}},\"content\":\"primary\"},{\"access\":{\"material\":{\"text\":\"PDF\"},\"textual\":{\"text\":\"Use of high contrast between text and background color\"}},\"content\":\"primary\"}],\"accessibilityNote\":[{\"displayConstant\":\"Accessibility features\",\"material\":{\"text\":\"EBSCOhost\"},\"summary\":{\"text\":\"\\\"EBSCO evaluates our products based on the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) and the related Section 508 and EN 301 549 regulations in the US and EU. Most EBSCO products are substantially conformant with WCAG 2.2 level AA.\\\" Source: https://connect.ebsco.com/s/article/EBSCO-VPATs?language=en_US. Last accessed April 22, 2025.\"}},{\"material\":{\"text\":\"PDF\"},\"summary\":{\"text\":\"Accessibility summary: This PDF has been created in accordance with the PDF/UA-1 standard to enhance accessibility, including screen reader support, described non-text content (images, graphs), bookmarks for easy navigation, keyboard-friendly links and forms and searchable, selectable text. We recognize the importance of accessibility, and we welcome queries about accessibility for any of our products. If you have a question or an access need, please get in touch with us at accessibilitysupport@springernature.com. Please note that a more accessible version of this eBook is available as ePub.\"}},{\"material\":{\"text\":\"PDF\"},\"summary\":{\"text\":\"No reading system accessibility options actively disabled\"}},{\"material\":{\"text\":\"PDF\"},\"summary\":{\"text\":\"Publisher contact for further accessibility information: accessibilitysupport@springernature.com\"}}],\"catalogingLanguage\":\"eng\",\"citationUrl\":\"https://www.oreilly.com/library/view/-/9798868818202/\",\"contributors\":[{\"firstName\":{\"text\":\"Regine M.\"},\"isPrimary\":true,\"relatorCodes\":[\"aut\"],\"secondName\":{\"text\":\"Gilbert\"}},{\"firstName\":{\"text\":\"Spandita\"},\"isPrimary\":false,\"relatorCodes\":[\"writer of foreword.\"],\"secondName\":{\"text\":\"Sarmah\"}}],\"creator\":\"Regine M. Gilbert\",\"date\":\"2025\",\"doi\":\"10.1007/979-8-8688-1820-2\",\"edition\":\"Second edition\",\"generalFormat\":\"Book\",\"incorrectIsbns\":[\"9798868818196\"],\"isBookReview\":false,\"isNewsArticle\":false,\"isbns\":[\"9798868818202\"],\"language\":\"eng\",\"machineReadableDate\":\"2025\",\"oclcNumber\":\"1548304168\",\"peerReviewed\":\"N\",\"publicationPlace\":\"New York, NY\",\"publisher\":\"Apress\",\"series\":\"Design thinking series\",\"specificFormat\":\"Digital\",\"subjectsText\":[\"Web-based user interfaces\",\"Accessible Web sites for people with disabilities\",\"Assistive computer technology\",\"Interfaces Web\",\"Sites Web accessibles aux personnes handicapées\",\"Technologie informatique adaptée\"],\"summariesText\":[\"Approach digital design with care, curiosity, and the people most often left out. This book invites you to rethink how we create digital systems, products, and tools, not just to meet accessibility requirements, but to shape a more inclusive future. UX design professor and author Regine Gilbert provides a thoughtful, practical, and global perspective on designing with empathy and intention across websites, apps, games, and emerging technologies like AI, VR, and AR. This expanded edition reflects the rapid evolution of the tech landscape. It features up-to-date guidance on the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG 2.2), the European Accessibility Act, and international standards. It also explores the intersection of AI and accessibility, examining both the promises and risks of machine learning, automated tools, and algorithmic bias. You'll learn how to ask better questions, challenge assumptions, and design for real human experiences, especially for those historically excluded. Inclusive Design for a Digital World, Second Edition isn't a checklist or a fix-it manual, it's a collection of reflections, case studies, questions, and examples that help you design with more people in mind from the start. Whether you're working on a subway kiosk, an AI chatbot, a learning app, or a video game, inclusive design is about recognizing who's being left out and doing the work to build systems that allow more people to participate, contribute, and belong. What You Will Learn: Apply WCAG 2.2 and understand how to meet international compliance requirements [if !supportLineBreakNewLine] [endif] Navigate the European Accessibility Act (EAA) and its implications for digital products [if !supportLineBreakNewLine] [endif] Design inclusive experiences for users with visual, motor, auditory, and cognitive disabilities [if !supportLineBreakNewLine] [endif] Identify how AI and machine learning impact accessibility and inclusion--both positively and negatively [if !supportLineBreakNewLine] [endif] Incorporate assistive technologies into your design and testing workflows [if !supportLineBreakNewLine] [endif] Create accessible mobile apps, websites, video games, and immersive experiences like VR and AR [if !supportLineBreakNewLine] [endif] Conduct user research and usability testing with diverse participants [if !supportLineBreakNewLine] [endif] Build inclusive design systems and content architectures from the ground up Who This Book Is For Designers, developers, researchers, product managers, content strategists, educators, and technologists working to embed inclusion into every phase of the digital product lifecycle, with a special emphasis on those exploring the impact of AI on accessibility\"],\"title\":\"Inclusive design for a digital world : designing with accessibility in mind\",\"titleInfo\":{\"text\":\"Inclusive design for a digital world : designing with accessibility in mind\"}}},{\"id\":951150513,\"itemType\":\"BibRecordSummary\",\"title\":\"Accessibility for persons with disabilities and the inclusive future of libraries\",\"creator\":\"John Carlo Bertot\",\"publicationDate\":\"2015\",\"itemRecord\":{\"catalogingLanguage\":\"eng\",\"contributors\":[{\"firstName\":{\"text\":\"John Carlo\"},\"isPrimary\":false,\"relatorCodes\":[\"edt\"],\"secondName\":{\"text\":\"Bertot\"}},{\"contributorNotes\":{\"date\":[\"1974-\"]},\"firstName\":{\"text\":\"Paul T.\"},\"isPrimary\":false,\"relatorCodes\":[\"edt\"],\"secondName\":{\"text\":\"Jaeger\"}},{\"firstName\":{\"text\":\"Brian\"},\"isPrimary\":false,\"relatorCodes\":[\"edt\"],\"secondName\":{\"text\":\"Wentz\"}}],\"creator\":\"John Carlo Bertot\",\"date\":\"2015\",\"generalFormat\":\"Book\",\"incorrectIsbns\":[\"9781785606526\"],\"isBookReview\":false,\"isNewsArticle\":false,\"isbns\":[\"9781785606533\",\"1785606530\"],\"language\":\"eng\",\"machineReadableDate\":\"2015\",\"mergedOclcNumbers\":[\"914573484\",\"914591867\",\"933503971\"],\"oclcNumber\":\"951150513\",\"peerReviewed\":\"N\",\"publicationPlace\":\"United Kingdom\",\"publisher\":\"Emerald Publishing\",\"series\":\"Advances in librarianship\",\"seriesVolumes\":[\"40\"],\"specificFormat\":\"PrintBook\",\"subjectsText\":[\"Libraries and people with disabilities\",\"Libraries Barrier-free design\",\"Bibliothèques et personnes handicapées\",\"Bibliothèques Accessibilité aux personnes handicapées\"],\"summariesText\":[\"All libraries have patrons and staff members with disabilities, making equitable service a priority for these organizations as they provide diverse services to their entire communities. Although rapid technological changes in recent years have offered challenges to libraries, these same technologies provide opportunities to embrace the concept of accessible library services and create innovative new services for patrons with disabilities. Accessibility for Persons with Disabilities and the Inclusive Future of Libraries, edited by Brian Wentz, Paul T. Jaeger, and John Carlo Bertot, focuses on the issues at the intersection of disability, accessibility, inclusion and libraries. The chapters in this volume provide best practices and innovative ideas to share amongst libraries, explore the roles that internet and communication technologies play in the context of inclusive libraries, illuminate the important contributions of libraries in promoting social inclusion of and social justice for people with disabilities, and help libraries to better articulate their contributions in these areas as they engage with disability groups, funders, policymakers, and other parts of their communities\"],\"title\":\"Accessibility for persons with disabilities and the inclusive future of libraries\",\"titleInfo\":{\"text\":\"Accessibility for persons with disabilities and the inclusive future of libraries\"}}},{\"id\":1402812750,\"itemType\":\"BibRecordSummary\",\"title\":\"What every engineer should know about digital accessibility\",\"creator\":\"Sarah Horton\",\"publicationDate\":\"2024\",\"itemRecord\":{\"catalogingLanguage\":\"eng\",\"contributors\":[{\"contributorNotes\":{\"date\":[\"1962-\"]},\"firstName\":{\"text\":\"Sarah\"},\"isPrimary\":true,\"relatorCodes\":[\"aut\"],\"secondName\":{\"text\":\"Horton\"}},{\"contributorNotes\":{\"note\":[\"(Writer on digital accessibility),\"]},\"firstName\":{\"text\":\"David\"},\"isPrimary\":false,\"relatorCodes\":[\"aut\"],\"secondName\":{\"text\":\"Sloan\"}}],\"creator\":\"Sarah Horton\",\"date\":\"2024\",\"edition\":\"First edition\",\"generalFormat\":\"Book\",\"incorrectIsbns\":[\"9781003288060\"],\"isBookReview\":false,\"isNewsArticle\":false,\"isbns\":[\"9781032263854\",\"1032263857\",\"9781032263861\",\"1032263865\"],\"language\":\"eng\",\"machineReadableDate\":\"2024\",\"mergedOclcNumbers\":[\"1402811232\",\"1538104357\"],\"oclcNumber\":\"1402812750\",\"peerReviewed\":\"N\",\"publicationPlace\":\"Boca Raton\",\"publisher\":\"CRC Press, Taylor & Francis Group\",\"series\":\"What every engineer should know\",\"specificFormat\":\"PrintBook\",\"subjectsText\":[\"Software engineering Social aspects\",\"Software engineering Moral and ethical aspects\",\"Computers and people with disabilities\",\"Technology and people with disabilities\",\"Computer software Human factors\",\"Computer software Development\",\"Software architecture Social aspects\",\"User interfaces (Computer systems)\",\"Génie logiciel Aspect social\",\"Ordinateurs et personnes handicapées\",\"Logiciels Facteurs humains\",\"Interfaces utilisateurs (Informatique)\",\"Génie logiciel Aspect moral\",\"Architecture logicielle Aspect social\"],\"summariesText\":[\"\\\"Accessibility is a core quality of digital products to be deliberately addressed throughout the development lifecycle. What Every Engineer Should Know About Digital Accessibility will prepare readers to integrate digital accessibility into their engineering practices. Readers will learn how to accurately frame accessibility as an engineering challenge so they are able to address the correct problems in the correct way. Illustrated with diverse perspectives from accessibility practitioners and advocates, this book describes how people with disabilities use technology, the nature of accessibility barriers in the digital world, and the role of engineers in breaking down those barriers. Accessibility competence for current, emerging, and future technologies is addressed through a combination of guiding principles, core attributes and requirements, and accessibility-informed engineering practices\\\"-- Back cover\"],\"title\":\"What every engineer should know about digital accessibility\",\"titleInfo\":{\"text\":\"What every engineer should know about digital accessibility\"}}},{\"id\":1512666121,\"itemType\":\"BibRecordSummary\",\"title\":\"The digital accessibility handbook for libraries\",\"creator\":\"Carli Spina\",\"publicationDate\":\"2025\",\"itemRecord\":{\"catalogingLanguage\":\"eng\",\"contributors\":[{\"firstName\":{\"text\":\"Carli\"},\"isPrimary\":true,\"relatorCodes\":[\"aut\"],\"secondName\":{\"text\":\"Spina\"}},{\"contributorNotes\":{\"date\":[\"1968-\"]},\"firstName\":{\"text\":\"Rebecca Albrecht\"},\"isPrimary\":false,\"relatorCodes\":[\"aut\"],\"secondName\":{\"text\":\"Oling\"}}],\"creator\":\"Carli Spina\",\"date\":\"2025\",\"generalFormat\":\"Book\",\"incorrectIsbns\":[\"9798892553148\",\"9798892553155\"],\"isBookReview\":false,\"isNewsArticle\":false,\"isbns\":[\"9798892552868\"],\"language\":\"eng\",\"machineReadableDate\":\"2025\",\"mergedOclcNumbers\":[\"1500055298\",\"1558008485\"],\"oclcNumber\":\"1512666121\",\"peerReviewed\":\"N\",\"publicationPlace\":\"Chicago\",\"publisher\":\"ALA Editions in collaboration with Core\",\"specificFormat\":\"PrintBook\",\"subjectsText\":[\"Libraries and people with disabilities United States\",\"Electronic information resources United States\",\"Library resources United States\",\"Computers and people with disabilities United States\",\"Accessible Web sites for people with disabilities\",\"Assistive computer technology\",\"Universal design\",\"Bibliothèques et personnes handicapées États-Unis\",\"Sources d'information électroniques États-Unis\",\"Fonds documentaires États-Unis\",\"Ordinateurs et personnes handicapées États-Unis\",\"Sites Web accessibles aux personnes handicapées\",\"Technologie informatique adaptée\",\"Conception universelle\",\"Libraries and people with disabilities\",\"Electronic information resources\",\"Library resources\",\"Computers and people with disabilities\",\"Instructional and educational works\",\"Matériel d'éducation et de formation\"],\"summariesText\":[\"\\\"In this book, authors dive into digital accessibility in libraries, starting with background information on understanding what is meant by disability and the obligations libraries have to support disabled users\\\"-- Provided by publisher\"],\"title\":\"The digital accessibility handbook for libraries\",\"titleInfo\":{\"text\":\"The digital accessibility handbook for libraries\"}}},{\"id\":1417759218,\"itemType\":\"BibRecordSummary\",\"title\":\"Making the library accessible for all : a practical guide for librarians\",\"creator\":\"Jane Vincent\",\"publicationDate\":\"2024\",\"itemRecord\":{\"catalogingLanguage\":\"eng\",\"contributors\":[{\"firstName\":{\"text\":\"Jane\"},\"isPrimary\":true,\"relatorCodes\":[\"aut\"],\"secondName\":{\"text\":\"Vincent\"}}],\"creator\":\"Jane Vincent\",\"date\":\"2024\",\"edition\":\"Second edition\",\"generalFormat\":\"Book\",\"incorrectIsbns\":[\"9781538176825\"],\"isBookReview\":false,\"isNewsArticle\":false,\"isbns\":[\"9781538176818\",\"1538176815\"],\"language\":\"eng\",\"machineReadableDate\":\"2024\",\"mergedOclcNumbers\":[\"1411030698\",\"1463334639\"],\"oclcNumber\":\"1417759218\",\"peerReviewed\":\"N\",\"publicationPlace\":\"Lanham, Maryland\",\"publisher\":\"Rowman & Littlefield, an imprint of The Rowman & Littlefield Publishing Group, Inc.\",\"series\":\"Practical guides for librarians\",\"seriesVolumes\":[\"no. 81\"],\"specificFormat\":\"PrintBook\",\"subjectsText\":[\"Libraries and people with disabilities\",\"Libraries and people with disabilities United States\",\"Self-help devices for people with disabilities\",\"Assistive computer technology\",\"Bibliothèques et personnes handicapées\",\"Bibliothèques et personnes handicapées États-Unis\",\"Aides fonctionnelles (Médecine physique)\",\"Technologie informatique adaptée\",\"LANGUAGE ARTS & DISCIPLINES / Communication Studies\",\"United States\"],\"summariesText\":[\"\\\"Making the Library Accessible for All is a single-source guide that librarians can refer to when planning, remediating, or evaluating ways to ensure disabled patrons and employees will have successful library experiences. It covers accessibility of communication, hard copy and electronic materials, architecture, trainings and events, technology access, website standards, and a range of related topics\\\"-- Provided by publisher\"],\"title\":\"Making the library accessible for all : a practical guide for librarians\",\"titleInfo\":{\"text\":\"Making the library accessible for all : a practical guide for librarians\"}}},{\"id\":1419271880,\"itemType\":\"BibRecordSummary\",\"title\":\"Web accessibility cookbook : creating inclusive experiences\",\"creator\":\"Manuel Matuzović\",\"publicationDate\":\"2024\",\"itemRecord\":{\"catalogingLanguage\":\"eng\",\"citationUrl\":\"https://www.oreilly.com/library/view/-/9781098145590/\",\"contributors\":[{\"firstName\":{\"text\":\"Manuel\"},\"isPrimary\":true,\"relatorCodes\":[\"aut\"],\"secondName\":{\"text\":\"Matuzović\"}}],\"creator\":\"Manuel Matuzović\",\"date\":\"2024\",\"edition\":\"First edition\",\"generalFormat\":\"Book\",\"incorrectIsbns\":[\"9781098145606\",\"1098145607\"],\"isBookReview\":false,\"isNewsArticle\":false,\"isbns\":[\"9781098145569\",\"1098145569\",\"9781098145576\",\"1098145577\"],\"language\":\"eng\",\"machineReadableDate\":\"2024\",\"mergedOclcNumbers\":[\"1440030078\",\"1459766151\"],\"oclcNumber\":\"1419271880\",\"peerReviewed\":\"N\",\"publicationPlace\":\"Sebastopol, CA\",\"publisher\":\"O'Reilly Media, Inc.\",\"specificFormat\":\"Digital\",\"subjectsText\":[\"Accessible Web sites for people with disabilities\",\"Computers and people with disabilities\",\"Web site development\",\"Web sites Barrier-free design\",\"Sites Web accessibles aux personnes handicapées\",\"Ordinateurs et personnes handicapées\",\"Sites Web Développement\",\"Sites Web Accessibilité aux personnes handicapées\"],\"summariesText\":[\"\\\"Frontend developers have to consider many things: browser compatibility, usability, performance, scalability, SEO, and other best practices. But the most fundamental aspect of creating websites is one that often falls short: accessibility. Accessibility is the cornerstone of any website, and if a website is inaccessible, users won't be able to interact with it, obtain information, sign up for services, or buy products. The Web Accessibility Cookbook provides you with dozens of recipes to help you avoid these failures. You'll learn how to build common components, such as main navigation, filters, and dialogs, in an accessible manner. Each recipe not only explains how to build things but also why. Author Manuel Matuzovic provides the knowledge you need to create your own accessible components and address your users' varying needs, abilities, and preferences.\\\"-- Provided by publisher\"],\"title\":\"Web accessibility cookbook : creating inclusive experiences\",\"titleInfo\":{\"text\":\"Web accessibility cookbook : creating inclusive experiences\"}}},{\"id\":1431047837,\"itemType\":\"BibRecordSummary\",\"title\":\"Practical web accessibility : a comprehensive guide to digital inclusion\",\"creator\":\"Ashley Firth\",\"publicationDate\":\"2024\",\"itemRecord\":{\"catalogingLanguage\":\"eng\",\"citationUrl\":\"https://www.oreilly.com/library/view/-/9798868801525/\",\"contributors\":[{\"firstName\":{\"text\":\"Ashley\"},\"isPrimary\":true,\"relatorCodes\":[\"aut\"],\"secondName\":{\"text\":\"Firth\"}}],\"creator\":\"Ashley Firth\",\"date\":\"2024\",\"doi\":\"10.1007/979-8-8688-0152-5\",\"edition\":\"2nd ed\",\"generalFormat\":\"Book\",\"incorrectIsbns\":[\"9798868801518\"],\"isBookReview\":false,\"isNewsArticle\":false,\"isbns\":[\"9798868801525\"],\"language\":\"eng\",\"machineReadableDate\":\"2024\",\"mergedOclcNumbers\":[\"1430685889\",\"1430755537\",\"1435492667\",\"1586932715\"],\"oclcNumber\":\"1431047837\",\"peerReviewed\":\"N\",\"publicationPlace\":\"London, UK\",\"publisher\":\"Apress\",\"series\":\"ITpro collection\",\"specificFormat\":\"Digital\",\"subjectsText\":[\"Accessible Web sites for people with disabilities\",\"Web sites Design\",\"World Wide Web Access control\",\"World Wide Web Social aspects\",\"Computers and people with disabilities\",\"Assistive computer technology\",\"Sites Web accessibles aux personnes handicapées\",\"Sites Web Conception\",\"Web Accès Contrôle\",\"Web Aspect social\",\"Ordinateurs et personnes handicapées\",\"Technologie informatique adaptée\"],\"summariesText\":[\"Everyone deserves to use the Internet. An estimated 1.3 billion people experience significant disability. That's 16percent of the world's population, or one in six of us. At the same time, over 96 percent of the one million most popular websites have an accessibility issue. Add to this the massive rise in legal cases around sites not being accessible, including Beyonce, Disney, and Netflix, and you have an important topic that more and more people are starting to engage with. In this updated and revamped second edition of the Amazon technology chart-topping Practical Web Accessibility, you'll be guided through a broad range of disabilities and access needs. You'll understand the ways these users typically engage with the web, the barriers they often face, and practical advice on how your websites and content can be compliant, but more than that, inclusive and enjoyable to use. There's also a new chapter on \\\"Outsourcing Accessibility,\\\" exploring third party \\\"bolt-on\\\" tools, \\\"build your own website\\\" platforms like Wix, and popular design systems. You'll explore whether they're helpful or detrimental in the fight to make the web more accessible.Throughout this book you'll learn to test for, spot, and fix web accessibility issues for a wide range of physical and mental impairments. Featuring content from the latest compliance frameworks, including the newly released WCAG 2.2 and exploratory concepts in WCAG 3, you'll see how to go beyond the basic requirements in order to help your users. You'll also learn that an accessible approach won't just help people with disabilities, it will improve your website for everyone. This book comes complete with practical examples you can use in your own sites, along with a brand-new approach to auditing and improving a website's accessibility, and a team's approach to it, based on tools created by the author and refined over years as a consultant -- The FAIR framework and ACCESS checklist. With these tools, you can set up processes for yourself and your team that will drastically improve the accessibility of your sites and, importantly, keep them that way in the future. Suitable for those of any profession or experience level, Practical Web Accessibility gives you all the information you need to ensure that your sites are truly accessible for the modern, inclusive web. If you would like to learn about web accessibility in a clear and actionable way, this book is for you. What You Will Learn A greater understanding of a vast range of disabilities that have online access needs, and the issues they typically face accessing content online. Ways to apply the practical steps required to cater for those needs. How to take your sites, and colleagues, on a journey from being inaccessible to accessible. The importance of accessibility in your designs, code, content, and more. The best ways to test and improve your sites, so you can be compliant, and truly accessible. Who This Book Is For Anyone, regardless of what they do, who wants to learn how to make websites and their content more accessible for those with disabilities. In the world of web, the book has been used by front and backend developers, designers, product and project managers, team and business leaders\"],\"title\":\"Practical web accessibility : a comprehensive guide to digital inclusion\",\"titleInfo\":{\"text\":\"Practical web accessibility : a comprehensive guide to digital inclusion\"}}}]}],\"fetchedData\":{\"listMetadata\":{\"id\":\"40adb58c-db5f-4f2d-9de3-5163b8651f9a\",\"displayOwner\":{\"nameVisible\":true},\"listName\":\"Global Accessibility Awareness Day 2026\",\"description\":\"Global Accessibility Awareness Day (GAAD) is observed annually on the third Thursday in May. Check out these resources to learn how to improve digital products, web content, and apps, making them accessible to all.\",\"listType\":\"worldcat-org\",\"public\":true,\"countOfItems\":21,\"countOfFollowers\":8,\"created\":\"2026-05-12T17:46:11.432Z\",\"modified\":\"2026-05-20T13:58:35.250Z\",\"modifiedBy\":\"SaraP\",\"ownerRegistryId\":268401},\"items\":[{\"id\":11181613916,\"itemType\":\"BibRecordSummary\",\"title\":\"Accessibility metadata: A journey to understanding and implementation\",\"creator\":\"Claire Holloway\",\"publicationDate\":\"2026\",\"itemRecord\":{\"citationUrl\":\"https://dx.doi.org/10.1177/18758789261435328\",\"contributors\":[{\"firstName\":{\"text\":\"Claire\"},\"isPrimary\":true,\"secondName\":{\"text\":\"Holloway\"}},{\"firstName\":{\"text\":\"Emily\"},\"isPrimary\":false,\"secondName\":{\"text\":\"Gilreath\"}},{\"firstName\":{\"text\":\"Morris\"},\"isPrimary\":false,\"secondName\":{\"text\":\"Levy\"}},{\"firstName\":{\"text\":\"Timothy\"},\"isPrimary\":false,\"secondName\":{\"text\":\"Savage\"}}],\"creator\":\"Claire Holloway\",\"date\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.1177/18758789261435328\",\"generalFormat\":\"ArtChap\",\"isBookReview\":false,\"isNewsArticle\":false,\"machineReadableDate\":\"2026\",\"oclcNumber\":\"11181613916\",\"peerReviewed\":\"Y\",\"source\":[{\"publicationInformation\":\"Sage UK: London, England, SAGE Publications\",\"relatedParts\":[\"v46 n1-2 (202605): 28-40\"],\"sourceIssn\":\"0167-5265\",\"sourceTitle\":\"Information Services and Use\"},{\"firstPages\":[\"28\"],\"issueDates\":[\"202605\"],\"issueDatesNormalized\":[\"202605\"],\"issues\":[\"1-2\"],\"pageRanges\":[\"28-40\"],\"volumes\":[\"46\"]}],\"sourceIssns\":[\"0167-5265\",\"1875-8789\"],\"specificFormat\":\"Artcl\",\"subjectsText\":[\"European Accessibility Act\",\"metadata\",\"OCLC\",\"ONIX\",\"MARC records\",\"W3C EPUB Accessibility\",\"information accessibility\",\"standards\"],\"summariesText\":[\"This paper is based upon the OCLC presentation at the February 2025 NISO Plus conference. It describes the organization’s journey to research compliance to the European Accessibility Act (EAA). It focuses on the three major complications that shaped their approach: the tension between internal and external metadata sources, the challenge of translating between different metadata formats, and the balance between controlled vocabularies and descriptive flexibility. Their investigation began with three questions: What metadata does the EAA actually require? How will this information flow through existing supply chains? And where should accessibility data be recorded in MARC records to best serve users. OCLC’s journey unearthed a complex landscape involving questions of trust between publishers and libraries, the limitations of existing standards, and the fundamental tension between textual description and systematic discovery. They hope that sharing these experiences will help other organizations navigate similar challenges more efficiently, while contributing to the broader efforts to standardize accessibility metadata that benefit the entire community of libraries, publishers, and content aggregators\"],\"title\":\"Accessibility metadata: A journey to understanding and implementation\",\"titleInfo\":{\"text\":\"Accessibility metadata: A journey to understanding and implementation\"}}},{\"id\":1228511736,\"itemType\":\"BibRecordSummary\",\"title\":\"Building For Everyone\",\"creator\":\"Annie Jean-Baptiste\",\"publicationDate\":\"2020\",\"itemRecord\":{\"catalogingLanguage\":\"eng\",\"citationUrl\":\"https://ezproxy.torontopubliclibrary.ca/login?url=https://learning.oreilly.com/library/view/-/9781119646228/\",\"contributors\":[{\"firstName\":{\"text\":\"Annie\"},\"isPrimary\":true,\"relatorCodes\":[\"aut\"],\"secondName\":{\"text\":\"Jean-Baptiste\"}},{\"isPrimary\":false,\"nonPersonName\":{\"text\":\"O'Reilly for Higher Education (Firm)\"},\"relatorCodes\":[\"dst\"]},{\"isPrimary\":false,\"nonPersonName\":{\"text\":\"Safari, an O'Reilly Media Company\"}},{\"isPrimary\":false,\"nonPersonName\":{\"text\":\"John Wiley & Sons\"},\"relatorCodes\":[\"pbl\"]}],\"creator\":\"Annie Jean-Baptiste\",\"date\":\"2020\",\"edition\":\"1st edition\",\"generalFormat\":\"Book\",\"isBookReview\":false,\"isNewsArticle\":false,\"isbns\":[\"9781119646228\",\"1119646227\"],\"language\":\"eng\",\"machineReadableDate\":\"2020\",\"oclcNumber\":\"1228511736\",\"peerReviewed\":\"N\",\"publicationPlace\":\"[Place of publication not identified]\",\"publisher\":\"Wiley\",\"specificFormat\":\"Digital\",\"subjectsText\":[\"Product design\",\"Universal design\",\"Conception de produit\",\"Conception universelle\"],\"summariesText\":[\"Diversity and Inclusion to build better products from the front lines at Google Establishing diverse and inclusive organizations is an economic imperative for every industry. Any business that isn't reaching a diverse market is missing out on enormous revenue potential and the opportunity to build products that suit their users' core needs. The economic \\\"why\\\" has been firmly established, but what about the \\\"how?\\\" How can business leaders adapt to our ever-more-diverse world by capturing market share AND building more inclusive products for people of color, women and other underrepresented groups? The Product Inclusion Team at Google has developed strategies to do just that and Building For Everyone is the practical guide to following in their footsteps. This book makes publicly available for the first time the same inclusive design process used at Google to create user-centric award-winning and profitable products. Author and Head of Product Inclusion Annie Jean-Baptiste outlines what those practices look like in industries beyond tech with fascinating case studies. Readers will learn the key strategies and step-by-step processes for inclusive product design that limits risk and increases profitability. Discover the questions you should be asking about diversity and inclusion in your products for marketers, user researchers, product managers and more. Understand the research the Product Inclusion team drove to back up their practices Learn the \\\"ABCs of Product Inclusion\\\" to build inclusion into your organization's culture Leverage the product inclusion suite of tools to get your organization building more inclusively and identifying new opportunities. Read case studies to see how product inclusion works across industries and learn what doesn't work. Building For Everyone will show you how to infuse your business processes with inclusive design. You'll learn best practices for inclusion in product design, marketing, management, leadership and beyond, straight from the innovative Google Product Inclusion team\"],\"title\":\"Building For Everyone\",\"titleInfo\":{\"text\":\"Building For Everyone\"}}},{\"id\":1523834436,\"itemType\":\"BibRecordSummary\",\"title\":\"Agile accessibility handbook : a practical guide to accessible software development at scale\",\"creator\":\"Dylan Barrell\",\"publicationDate\":\"2020\",\"itemRecord\":{\"catalogingLanguage\":\"eng\",\"contributors\":[{\"firstName\":{\"text\":\"Dylan\"},\"isPrimary\":true,\"secondName\":{\"text\":\"Barrell\"}}],\"creator\":\"Dylan Barrell\",\"date\":\"2020\",\"generalFormat\":\"Book\",\"isBookReview\":false,\"isNewsArticle\":false,\"isbns\":[\"9781645434771\",\"164543477X\"],\"language\":\"eng\",\"machineReadableDate\":\"2020\",\"oclcNumber\":\"1523834436\",\"peerReviewed\":\"N\",\"publicationPlace\":\"Herndon, VA\",\"publisher\":\"Amplify Publishing\",\"specificFormat\":\"PrintBook\",\"subjectsText\":[\"People with disabilities Web applications\",\"Accessible Web sites for people with disabilities\",\"Assistive computer technology\",\"Sites Web accessibles aux personnes handicapées\",\"Technologie informatique adaptée\",\"handbooks\",\"Handbooks and manuals\",\"Guides et manuels\"],\"summariesText\":[\"\\\"It is estimated that one in five people has a disability; if you do the math, that's a huge, addressable market that is often overlooked. Digital Accessibility practitioners tap into this market by making digital documents as well as web and mobile apps accessible to everyone. However, many enterprises struggle to create, maintain, and scale their digital accessibility efforts. Agile Accessibility Handbook outlines the steps organizations can take to capture this market, avoid risk, maintain agility, and close the accessibility gap. Using the information provided within this handbook, accessibility subject matter experts, development team members, and executives in charge of setting priorities can together learn how to build successful accessibility experiences for everyone.\\\"--amazon.com\"],\"title\":\"Agile accessibility handbook : a practical guide to accessible software development at scale\",\"titleInfo\":{\"text\":\"Agile accessibility handbook : a practical guide to accessible software development at scale\"}}},{\"id\":1025413063,\"itemType\":\"BibRecordSummary\",\"title\":\"Mismatch : how inclusion shapes design\",\"creator\":\"Kat Holmes\",\"publicationDate\":\"2018\",\"itemRecord\":{\"catalogingLanguage\":\"eng\",\"contributors\":[{\"firstName\":{\"text\":\"Kat\"},\"isPrimary\":true,\"relatorCodes\":[\"aut\"],\"secondName\":{\"text\":\"Holmes\"}}],\"creator\":\"Kat Holmes\",\"date\":\"2018\",\"generalFormat\":\"Book\",\"isBookReview\":false,\"isNewsArticle\":false,\"isbns\":[\"9780262038881\",\"0262038889\",\"9780262539487\",\"0262539489\"],\"language\":\"eng\",\"machineReadableDate\":\"2018\",\"mergedOclcNumbers\":[\"1029652413\",\"1029788823\",\"1029849282\",\"1493275828\"],\"oclcNumber\":\"1025413063\",\"peerReviewed\":\"N\",\"publicationPlace\":\"Cambridge, Massachusetts\",\"publisher\":\"The MIT Press\",\"series\":\"Simplicity (Cambridge, Mass.)\",\"specificFormat\":\"PrintBook\",\"subjectsText\":[\"Design Anthropological aspects\",\"Social integration\",\"Marginality, Social\",\"Social Integration\",\"Design Aspect anthropologique\",\"Intégration sociale\"],\"summariesText\":[\"\\\"Sometimes designed objects reject their users: a computer mouse that doesn't work for left-handed people, for example, or a touchscreen payment system that only works for people who read English phrases, have 20/20 vision, and use a credit card. Something as simple as color choices can render a product unusable for millions. These mismatches are the building blocks of exclusion. In Mismatch, Kat Holmes describes how design can lead to exclusion, and how design can also remedy exclusion. Inclusive design methods--designing objects with rather than for excluded users--can create elegant solutions that work well and benefit all. Holmes tells stories of pioneers of inclusive design, many of whom were drawn to work on inclusion because of their own experiences of exclusion. A gamer and designer who depends on voice recognition shows Holmes his 'Wall of Exclusion, ' which displays dozens of game controllers that require two hands to operate; an architect shares her firsthand knowledge of how design can fail communities, gleaned from growing up in Detroit's housing projects; an astronomer who began to lose her eyesight adapts a technique called 'sonification' so she can 'listen' to the stars. Designing for inclusion is not a feel-good sideline. Holmes shows how inclusion can be a source of innovation and growth, especially for digital technologies. It can be a catalyst for creativity and a boost for the bottom line as a customer base expands. And each time we remedy a mismatched interaction, we create an opportunity for more people to contribute to society in meaningful ways.\\\"--Publisher's description\"],\"title\":\"Mismatch : how inclusion shapes design\",\"titleInfo\":{\"text\":\"Mismatch : how inclusion shapes design\"}}},{\"id\":1569680396,\"itemType\":\"BibRecordSummary\",\"title\":\"Accessible UX research\",\"creator\":\"Michele A. Williams\",\"publicationDate\":\"2025\",\"itemRecord\":{\"accessibilityNote\":[{\"displayConstant\":\"Accessibility features\",\"material\":{\"text\":\"EBSCOhost\"},\"summary\":{\"text\":\"\\\"EBSCO evaluates our products based on the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) and the related Section 508 and EN 301 549 regulations in the US and EU. Most EBSCO products are substantially conformant with WCAG 2.2 level AA.\\\" Source: https://connect.ebsco.com/s/article/EBSCO-VPATs?language=en_US. Last accessed April 22, 2025.\"}}],\"catalogingLanguage\":\"eng\",\"citationUrl\":\"https://search.ebscohost.com/login.aspx?direct=true&scope=site&db=nlebk&db=nlabk&AN=4407870\",\"contributors\":[{\"firstName\":{\"text\":\"Michele A.\"},\"isPrimary\":true,\"secondName\":{\"text\":\"Williams\"}}],\"creator\":\"Michele A. Williams\",\"date\":\"2025\",\"generalFormat\":\"Book\",\"isBookReview\":false,\"isNewsArticle\":false,\"isbns\":[\"9783910835030\",\"3910835031\",\"9783910835047\",\"391083504X\"],\"language\":\"eng\",\"machineReadableDate\":\"2025\",\"mergedOclcNumbers\":[\"1569333684\"],\"oclcNumber\":\"1569680396\",\"peerReviewed\":\"N\",\"publicationPlace\":\"[Place of publication not identified]\",\"publisher\":\"Smashing Magazine\",\"specificFormat\":\"Digital\",\"subjectsText\":[\"User interfaces (Computer systems)\",\"Interfaces utilisateurs (Informatique)\"],\"title\":\"Accessible UX research\",\"titleInfo\":{\"text\":\"Accessible UX research\"}}},{\"id\":1475275030,\"itemType\":\"BibRecordSummary\",\"title\":\"Accessible communications : create impact, avoid missteps and build trust\",\"creator\":\"Lisa Riemers\",\"publicationDate\":\"2026\",\"itemRecord\":{\"catalogingLanguage\":\"eng\",\"contributors\":[{\"firstName\":{\"text\":\"Lisa\"},\"isPrimary\":true,\"relatorCodes\":[\"aut\"],\"secondName\":{\"text\":\"Riemers\"}},{\"firstName\":{\"text\":\"Matisse\"},\"isPrimary\":false,\"relatorCodes\":[\"aut\"],\"secondName\":{\"text\":\"Hamel-Nelis\"}}],\"creator\":\"Lisa Riemers\",\"date\":\"2026\",\"generalFormat\":\"Book\",\"incorrectIsbns\":[\"9781398621855\"],\"isBookReview\":false,\"isNewsArticle\":false,\"isbns\":[\"9781398621848\",\"1398621846\",\"9781398621862\",\"1398621862\"],\"language\":\"eng\",\"machineReadableDate\":\"2026\",\"mergedOclcNumbers\":[\"1475276359\"],\"oclcNumber\":\"1475275030\",\"peerReviewed\":\"N\",\"publicationPlace\":\"London\",\"publisher\":\"Kogan Page\",\"specificFormat\":\"PrintBook\",\"subjectsText\":[\"Business communication\",\"Public relations\",\"Social responsibility of business\",\"Communication dans l'entreprise\",\"Entreprises Responsabilité sociale\",\"Relations publiques\",\"public relations\"],\"summariesText\":[\"\\\"Overlooking accessibility can be expensive, but integrating it from the start amplifies reach and saves money in the long run. Accessible communications expand audiences, boost sales, protect reputations and ensure everyone can access information without exclusion. This practical and easy-to-follow guide ensures mid-level communicators feel confident in creating truly accessible communications across various formats, from emails and documents to videos and social. With the emphasis on practical content examples that professionals encounter daily and a holistic approach, this book will become the ultimate companion to anyone looking to communicate information effectively. Whether that's internal communications for colleagues or external messages for customers, suppliers, shareholders or other stakeholders. Written by two leading communications consultants who provide in-depth coverage of evolving legislation in the area and a forward-looking approach that goes beyond compliance and looks towards clarity and inclusivity, this book equips communicators to develop communications that build business reputation and consumer trust. With real-world examples, this book ensures that all communications are inclusive and effective\\\"-- Provided by publisher\"],\"title\":\"Accessible communications : create impact, avoid missteps and build trust\",\"titleInfo\":{\"text\":\"Accessible communications : create impact, avoid missteps and build trust\"}}},{\"id\":1545067346,\"itemType\":\"BibRecordSummary\",\"title\":\"Digital accessibility ethics : disability inclusion in all things tech\",\"creator\":\"Lainey Feingold\",\"publicationDate\":\"2026\",\"itemRecord\":{\"catalogingLanguage\":\"eng\",\"contributors\":[{\"firstName\":{\"text\":\"Lainey\"},\"isPrimary\":false,\"relatorCodes\":[\"edt\"],\"secondName\":{\"text\":\"Feingold\"}},{\"firstName\":{\"text\":\"Reginé M.\"},\"isPrimary\":false,\"relatorCodes\":[\"edt\"],\"secondName\":{\"text\":\"Gilbert\"}},{\"firstName\":{\"text\":\"Chancey\"},\"isPrimary\":false,\"relatorCodes\":[\"edt\"],\"secondName\":{\"text\":\"Fleet\"}}],\"creator\":\"Lainey Feingold\",\"date\":\"2026\",\"edition\":\"First edition\",\"generalFormat\":\"Book\",\"incorrectIsbns\":[\"9781003616702\",\"9781040604762\",\"9781040571583\"],\"isBookReview\":false,\"isNewsArticle\":false,\"isbns\":[\"9781041018698\",\"104101869X\",\"9781041018681\",\"1041018681\"],\"language\":\"eng\",\"machineReadableDate\":\"2026\",\"mergedOclcNumbers\":[\"1545052283\",\"1593505474\"],\"oclcNumber\":\"1545067346\",\"peerReviewed\":\"N\",\"publicationPlace\":\"Boca Raton\",\"publisher\":\"CRC Press, Taylor & Francis Group\",\"specificFormat\":\"PrintBook\",\"subjectsText\":[\"Computers and people with disabilities\",\"Accessible Web sites for people with disabilities\",\"Digital divide\",\"People with disabilities Services for\",\"Computer software Development Moral and ethical aspects\",\"Information technology Moral and ethical aspects\",\"Ordinateurs et personnes handicapées\",\"Sites Web accessibles aux personnes handicapées\",\"Fossé numérique\",\"Personnes handicapées Services\",\"Computer software Development\"],\"summariesText\":[\"\\\"Digital Accessibility Ethics is a practical guide with an urgent goal: to help end tech exclusion of 1.3 billion people across the world with disabilities. The book introduces the first Digital Accessibility Ethics Framework - an action-oriented, three-part tool designed to influence, change, and disrupt patterns of exclusion with values, actions, and questions. 39 authors from 10 countries and one commonwealth, the majority of whom are disabled, apply this Framework across technologies, sectors, and countries. The editors and authors - with over 600 years of combined accessibility and disability advocacy experience -- aim to build a world that recognizes disabled people's right to fully participate in every facet of digital life. And to offer organizations an ethics lens to help eliminate the financial, legal, privacy, safety, and other risks and harms of disability exclusion. Through stories, recommendations, strategies, and other guidance, the book looks at a wide range of topics through an ethics lens: from gaming and smart cities to hackathons, procurement, and cybersecurity. From accessibility practitioner burnout, to robots, artificial intelligence, aerospace, design, healthcare, open source, emergency preparedness, legal ethics, publishing and much more. This book is for technologists, educators, students, marketers, policy makers and everyone who has ever posted on social media or sent an email. It encourages us to stop and ask ourselves: who are we excluding by our actions? Who are we harming, what are we risking, by our decisions? As the world grows more digital, as AI is marketed everywhere, and as the number of people with disabilities continues to grow, there has never been a more urgent time to expose, explore, and act at the intersection of ethics, disability, and digital accessibility. Digital Accessibility Ethics offers a roadmap to show us the way\\\"-- Provided by publisher\"],\"title\":\"Digital accessibility ethics : disability inclusion in all things tech\",\"titleInfo\":{\"text\":\"Digital accessibility ethics : disability inclusion in all things tech\"}}},{\"id\":1372499580,\"itemType\":\"BibRecordSummary\",\"title\":\"Guide to digital accessibility : policies, practices, and professional development\",\"creator\":\"Rae Mancilla\",\"publicationDate\":\"2023\",\"itemRecord\":{\"catalogingLanguage\":\"eng\",\"contributors\":[{\"firstName\":{\"text\":\"Rae\"},\"isPrimary\":false,\"relatorCodes\":[\"edt\"],\"secondName\":{\"text\":\"Mancilla\"}},{\"firstName\":{\"text\":\"Barbara A.\"},\"isPrimary\":false,\"relatorCodes\":[\"edt\"],\"secondName\":{\"text\":\"Frey\"}}],\"creator\":\"Rae Mancilla\",\"date\":\"2023\",\"edition\":\"First edition\",\"generalFormat\":\"Book\",\"incorrectIsbns\":[\"9781642674545\",\"9781642674552\"],\"isBookReview\":false,\"isNewsArticle\":false,\"isbns\":[\"9781642674521\",\"1642674524\",\"9781642674538\",\"1642674532\",\"1642674524\",\"9781642674521\"],\"language\":\"eng\",\"machineReadableDate\":\"2023\",\"mergedOclcNumbers\":[\"1352795713\",\"1352795895\"],\"oclcNumber\":\"1372499580\",\"peerReviewed\":\"N\",\"publicationPlace\":\"Sterling, Virginia\",\"publisher\":\"Stylus\",\"specificFormat\":\"PrintBook\",\"subjectsText\":[\"Internet in higher education\",\"Web-based instruction\",\"Internet dans l'enseignement supérieur\",\"Internet en la enseñanza superior\",\"Enseñanza en línea\"],\"summariesText\":[\"\\\"Written for practitioners by practitioners, this book addresses vital compliance issues and maps a range of proven practices that will create and enrich online learning experiences that are accessible and usable by all learners\\\"-- Provided by publisher\"],\"title\":\"Guide to digital accessibility : policies, practices, and professional development\",\"titleInfo\":{\"text\":\"Guide to digital accessibility : policies, practices, and professional development\"}}},{\"id\":1528630819,\"itemType\":\"BibRecordSummary\",\"title\":\"Inclusive design for accessibility : a practical guide to digital accessibility, UX, and inclusive web & app design\",\"creator\":\"Dale Cruse\",\"publicationDate\":\"2025\",\"itemRecord\":{\"accessibilityNote\":[{\"displayConstant\":\"Accessibility features\",\"material\":{\"text\":\"EBSCOhost\"},\"summary\":{\"text\":\"\\\"EBSCO evaluates our products based on the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) and the related Section 508 and EN 301 549 regulations in the US and EU. Most EBSCO products are substantially conformant with WCAG 2.2 level AA.\\\" Source: https://connect.ebsco.com/s/article/EBSCO-VPATs?language=en_US. Last accessed April 22, 2025\"}}],\"catalogingLanguage\":\"eng\",\"citationUrl\":\"https://search.ebscohost.com/login.aspx?direct=true&scope=site&db=nlebk&db=nlabk&AN=4270552\",\"contributors\":[{\"firstName\":{\"text\":\"Dale\"},\"isPrimary\":true,\"relatorCodes\":[\"aut\"],\"secondName\":{\"text\":\"Cruse\"}},{\"firstName\":{\"text\":\"Denis\"},\"isPrimary\":false,\"relatorCodes\":[\"aut\"],\"secondName\":{\"text\":\"Boudreau\"}}],\"creator\":\"Dale Cruse\",\"date\":\"2025\",\"generalFormat\":\"Book\",\"isBookReview\":false,\"isNewsArticle\":false,\"isbns\":[\"1835888232\",\"9781835888230\",\"1835888224\",\"9781835888223\"],\"language\":\"eng\",\"machineReadableDate\":\"2025\",\"oclcNumber\":\"1528630819\",\"peerReviewed\":\"N\",\"publicationPlace\":\"Birmingham\",\"publisher\":\"Packt Publishing\",\"specificFormat\":\"Digital\",\"subjectsText\":[\"Computer software Human factors\",\"Computers and people with disabilities\",\"Software engineering Social aspects\",\"Logiciels Facteurs humains\",\"Ordinateurs et personnes handicapées\",\"Génie logiciel Aspect social\",\"Software engineering\"],\"summariesText\":[\"\\\"In \\\"\\\"Inclusive Design for Accessibility,\\\"\\\" you'll learn how to create digital experiences that truly empower all users, regardless of their abilities. This book covers the principles of inclusive design, practical strategies, and real-world examples, helping you integrate accessibility into every step of your design and development process. What this Book will help me do Master the core principles of inclusive design to cater to a diverse audience. Develop accessible interfaces for various platforms including web, mobile, and emerging technologies. Conduct effective user research to better understand diverse needs and integrate accessibility insights. Leverage AI to improve and automate accessibility features in digital products. Foster an organizational culture that prioritizes accessibility and inclusive design. Author(s) Dale Cruse and Denis Boudreau are highly respected experts in the field of digital accessibility and inclusive design. Dale has extensive experience in user experience and interface design, while Denis is a recognized leader and consultant in accessibility advocacy and education. Together, they bring valuable expertise and hands-on strategies to help readers tackle real-world accessibility challenges. Who is it for? This book is ideal for digital professionals, including designers, developers, UX practitioners, and product managers, who aim to create inclusive digital products. It's suited for beginners to advanced practitioners eager to understand and implement accessibility. Additionally, it serves business leaders looking to foster accessibility in organizational culture and fulfill legal compliance.\\\"\"],\"title\":\"Inclusive design for accessibility : a practical guide to digital accessibility, UX, and inclusive web & app design\",\"titleInfo\":{\"text\":\"Inclusive design for accessibility : a practical guide to digital accessibility, UX, and inclusive web & app design\"}}},{\"id\":1131698037,\"itemType\":\"BibRecordSummary\",\"title\":\"Inclusive components : accessible web interfaces, piece by piece\",\"creator\":\"Heydon Pickering\",\"publicationDate\":\"2019\",\"itemRecord\":{\"catalogingLanguage\":\"eng\",\"contributors\":[{\"firstName\":{\"text\":\"Heydon\"},\"isPrimary\":true,\"relatorCodes\":[\"aut\"],\"secondName\":{\"text\":\"Pickering\"}}],\"creator\":\"Heydon Pickering\",\"date\":\"2019\",\"generalFormat\":\"Book\",\"isBookReview\":false,\"isNewsArticle\":false,\"isbns\":[\"9783945749821\",\"3945749824\"],\"language\":\"eng\",\"machineReadableDate\":\"2019\",\"oclcNumber\":\"1131698037\",\"peerReviewed\":\"N\",\"publicationPlace\":\"Freiburg, Germany\",\"publisher\":\"Smashing Magazine AG\",\"specificFormat\":\"PrintBook\",\"subjectsText\":[\"Web sites Design\",\"Accessible Web sites for people with disabilities\",\"Computers and people with disabilities\",\"Sites Web Conception\",\"Sites Web accessibles aux personnes handicapées\",\"Ordinateurs et personnes handicapées\"],\"summariesText\":[\"\\\"In his brand-new book Inclusive Components, Heydon Pickering explores more accessible and robust solutions for the UI patterns we author, plug in, and use every day. Written for front-end developers who want to detect and address potential accessibility issues in their components, you'll not only learn to see common web UI patterns through the lens of inclusion and adopt an inclusive mindset but practical code samples and working demos help you make a change right away.\\\"-- From Smashing Magazine website\"],\"title\":\"Inclusive components : accessible web interfaces, piece by piece\",\"titleInfo\":{\"text\":\"Inclusive components : accessible web interfaces, piece by piece\"}}},{\"id\":1494975796,\"itemType\":\"BibRecordSummary\",\"title\":\"Dark and Silent Office : A Digital Accessibility Guidebook for Inclusive Communication in the Workplace\",\"creator\":\"Stephanie Warlick\",\"publicationDate\":\"2024\",\"itemRecord\":{\"catalogingLanguage\":\"eng\",\"contributors\":[{\"firstName\":{\"text\":\"Stephanie\"},\"isPrimary\":true,\"relatorCodes\":[\"aut\"],\"secondName\":{\"text\":\"Warlick\"}},{\"firstName\":{\"text\":\"Glenda\"},\"isPrimary\":false,\"secondName\":{\"text\":\"Sims\"}}],\"creator\":\"Stephanie Warlick\",\"date\":\"2024\",\"generalFormat\":\"Book\",\"isBookReview\":false,\"isNewsArticle\":false,\"isbns\":[\"9798989821808\"],\"language\":\"eng\",\"machineReadableDate\":\"2024\",\"oclcNumber\":\"1494975796\",\"peerReviewed\":\"N\",\"publicationPlace\":\"[Place of publication not identified]\",\"publisher\":\"5FT View Consulting, LLC\",\"specificFormat\":\"PrintBook\",\"subjectsText\":[\"Accessible Web sites for people with disabilities Planning\",\"Computers and people with disabilities\",\"Technology and people with disabilities\",\"Assistive computer technology\",\"Sites Web accessibles aux personnes handicapées Planification\",\"Ordinateurs et personnes handicapées\",\"Technologie informatique adaptée\"],\"summariesText\":[\"Ask anyone and they would agree that technology is a necessary component of the workplace. But have you ever relied on technology and it failed -- just before your deadline? Think about having that experience all day, every day while attempting to meet your daily work objectives. There are approximately 37.5 million adults in the US with trouble hearing and another 50.18 million adults with some degree of vision loss. The fight for equity in the workplace has very much focused on gender and race, and while these steps are completely necessary, visually-disabled and hearing-disabled individuals are a minority group that is significantly overlooked. Jenny sat in a meeting where the manager was detailing the quarterly financial review. As they discussed the colors of charts and diagrams, Jenny, being colorblind, couldn't keep up. She left the meeting exhausted and deflated. Mark was typing away on his computer when the team leader informed the office about an important update. If it hadn't been for his colleague advising him, Mark, being deaf, would have missed out on this information. Nobody intentionally excludes the visually and hearing impaired. But that's not enough in the year 2024 where the benefits of inclusivity have been demonstrated time and time again. But there is a huge gap between wanting an inclusive workplace and actually achieving it. It's a gap that you find yourself standing in right now! The workplace is buzzing in a digital era and overall, technology is closing so many gaps across the industries. At the same time, it's sadly making the gap bigger for those with sight and hearing difficulties\"],\"title\":\"Dark and Silent Office : A Digital Accessibility Guidebook for Inclusive Communication in the Workplace\",\"titleInfo\":{\"text\":\"Dark and Silent Office : A Digital Accessibility Guidebook for Inclusive Communication in the Workplace\"}}},{\"id\":1518507037,\"itemType\":\"BibRecordSummary\",\"title\":\"The accessibility operations guidebook : to making accessibility work more sustainable\",\"creator\":\"Devon Persing\",\"publicationDate\":\"2025\",\"itemRecord\":{\"catalogingLanguage\":\"eng\",\"contributors\":[{\"firstName\":{\"text\":\"Devon\"},\"isPrimary\":true,\"relatorCodes\":[\"aut\"],\"secondName\":{\"text\":\"Persing\"}}],\"creator\":\"Devon Persing\",\"date\":\"2025\",\"edition\":\"First edition\",\"generalFormat\":\"Book\",\"isBookReview\":false,\"isNewsArticle\":false,\"isbns\":[\"9798307802304\"],\"language\":\"eng\",\"machineReadableDate\":\"2025\",\"oclcNumber\":\"1518507037\",\"peerReviewed\":\"N\",\"publicationPlace\":\"[S.l.]\",\"publisher\":\"ADMIT HUB REF SERVICE PR\",\"specificFormat\":\"PrintBook\",\"subjectsText\":[\"Digital accessibility\",\"Guidebook\",\"Assistive computer technology\",\"Technologie informatique adaptée\"],\"summariesText\":[\"\\\"The accessibility field has a burnout problem. People get into this work to make accessible products and services. But, they often find themselves doing a lot of other work - program management, legal compliance, and constant, constant advocacy - instead. This isn't usually what people sign up for, and it leads directly to burnout. / This book seeks to help break that cycle. It's not about accessibility work itself, but about building digital programs that are more sustainable, intersectional, and data-driven. / The first part of the book is a crash course in social science. It introduces theories about organizational psychology, community, education, information literacy, work burnout, disability, and intersectionality. / The second part is a strategy guide. It takes the theories from the first part and applies them to building an accessibility practice that better fits your needs and those of your organization. It's about using data and systems thinking to help you focus on the hard work of growing community, centering disability and disabled people, and enabling accessibility instead of policing it\"],\"title\":\"The accessibility operations guidebook : to making accessibility work more sustainable\",\"titleInfo\":{\"text\":\"The accessibility operations guidebook : to making accessibility work more sustainable\"}}},{\"id\":871042774,\"itemType\":\"BibRecordSummary\",\"title\":\"A web for everyone : designing accessible user experiences\",\"creator\":\"Sarah Horton\",\"publicationDate\":\"2013\",\"itemRecord\":{\"catalogingLanguage\":\"eng\",\"contributors\":[{\"contributorNotes\":{\"date\":[\"1962-\"]},\"firstName\":{\"text\":\"Sarah\"},\"isPrimary\":true,\"relatorCodes\":[\"aut\"],\"secondName\":{\"text\":\"Horton\"}},{\"firstName\":{\"text\":\"Whitney\"},\"isPrimary\":false,\"relatorCodes\":[\"aut\"],\"secondName\":{\"text\":\"Quesenbery\"}}],\"creator\":\"Sarah Horton\",\"date\":\"2013\",\"generalFormat\":\"Book\",\"isBookReview\":false,\"isNewsArticle\":false,\"isbns\":[\"9781933820972\",\"1933820977\"],\"language\":\"eng\",\"machineReadableDate\":\"2013\",\"oclcNumber\":\"871042774\",\"peerReviewed\":\"N\",\"publicationPlace\":\"Brooklyn, New York\",\"publisher\":\"Rosenfeld Media\",\"specificFormat\":\"PrintBook\",\"subjectsText\":[\"Accessible Web sites for people with disabilities\",\"Web site development\",\"Internet\",\"Human-computer interaction\",\"Sites Web accessibles aux personnes handicapées\",\"Sites Web Développement\"],\"summariesText\":[\"A Web for Everyone will help you make your site accessible without sacrificing design or innovation. Rooted in universal design principles, this book provides solutions: practical advice and examples of how to create sites that everyone can use\"],\"title\":\"A web for everyone : designing accessible user experiences\",\"titleInfo\":{\"text\":\"A web for everyone : designing accessible user experiences\"}}},{\"id\":1578999555,\"itemType\":\"BibRecordSummary\",\"title\":\"Digital outcasts : moving technology forward without leaving people behind\",\"creator\":\"Kel Smith\",\"publicationDate\":\"2026\",\"itemRecord\":{\"catalogingLanguage\":\"eng\",\"contributors\":[{\"firstName\":{\"text\":\"Kel\"},\"isPrimary\":true,\"relatorCodes\":[\"aut\"],\"secondName\":{\"text\":\"Smith\"}}],\"creator\":\"Kel Smith\",\"date\":\"2026\",\"edition\":\"Second edition\",\"generalFormat\":\"Book\",\"incorrectIsbns\":[\"9780443336782\"],\"isBookReview\":false,\"isNewsArticle\":false,\"isbns\":[\"9780443336775\",\"0443336776\"],\"language\":\"eng\",\"machineReadableDate\":\"2026\",\"oclcNumber\":\"1578999555\",\"peerReviewed\":\"N\",\"publicationPlace\":\"Amsterdam\",\"publisher\":\"Morgan Kaufmann Publisher, an imprint of Elsevier\",\"specificFormat\":\"PrintBook\",\"subjectsText\":[\"Assistive computer technology\",\"Computers and people with disabilities\",\"Technologie informatique adaptée\",\"Ordinateurs et personnes handicapées\"],\"summariesText\":[\"\\\"Comprehensively explores inclusive design in human-computer interaction. The book examines the real-life experiences of people with disabilities as they navigate systemic barriers in employment, education, healthcare, and social connectivity. This new edition covers the intersectionality of disability with other forms of economic and political discrimination, uncovering how biases related to race, gender, and ability are reflected in language models and AI algorithms. With digital access a foundational element of human existence, the consequences of exclusion are far-reaching and increasingly urgent. Citing case studies in law, creative arts, and social science, this updated edition also examines the historical and emergent impact people with disabilities have on culture and industry. Digital Outcasts emphases that disability has long served as a powerful catalyst for design innovation, driving transformational benefit for consumers of all abilities and backgrounds. Taking into account new legal and technological perspectives, this revision stands as an update on the progress we have made—and how far we have yet to go.\\\"--Publisher's website\"],\"title\":\"Digital outcasts : moving technology forward without leaving people behind\",\"titleInfo\":{\"text\":\"Digital outcasts : moving technology forward without leaving people behind\"}}},{\"id\":1548304168,\"itemType\":\"BibRecordSummary\",\"title\":\"Inclusive design for a digital world : designing with accessibility in mind\",\"creator\":\"Regine M. Gilbert\",\"publicationDate\":\"2025\",\"itemRecord\":{\"accessibilityContent\":[{\"access\":{\"material\":{\"text\":\"PDF\"},\"textual\":{\"text\":\"All non-decorative content supports reading without sight\"}},\"content\":\"primary\"},{\"access\":{\"material\":{\"text\":\"PDF\"},\"textual\":{\"text\":\"Next / Previous structural navigation\"}},\"content\":\"primary\"},{\"access\":{\"material\":{\"text\":\"PDF\"},\"textual\":{\"text\":\"PDF/UA-1\"}},\"content\":\"primary\"},{\"access\":{\"material\":{\"text\":\"PDF\"},\"textual\":{\"text\":\"Short alternative textual descriptions\"}},\"content\":\"primary\"},{\"access\":{\"material\":{\"text\":\"PDF\"},\"textual\":{\"text\":\"Single logical reading order\"}},\"content\":\"primary\"},{\"access\":{\"material\":{\"text\":\"PDF\"},\"textual\":{\"text\":\"Table of contents navigation\"}},\"content\":\"primary\"},{\"access\":{\"material\":{\"text\":\"PDF\"},\"textual\":{\"text\":\"Use of color is not sole means of conveying information\"}},\"content\":\"primary\"},{\"access\":{\"material\":{\"text\":\"PDF\"},\"textual\":{\"text\":\"Use of high contrast between text and background color\"}},\"content\":\"primary\"}],\"accessibilityNote\":[{\"displayConstant\":\"Accessibility features\",\"material\":{\"text\":\"EBSCOhost\"},\"summary\":{\"text\":\"\\\"EBSCO evaluates our products based on the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) and the related Section 508 and EN 301 549 regulations in the US and EU. Most EBSCO products are substantially conformant with WCAG 2.2 level AA.\\\" Source: https://connect.ebsco.com/s/article/EBSCO-VPATs?language=en_US. Last accessed April 22, 2025.\"}},{\"material\":{\"text\":\"PDF\"},\"summary\":{\"text\":\"Accessibility summary: This PDF has been created in accordance with the PDF/UA-1 standard to enhance accessibility, including screen reader support, described non-text content (images, graphs), bookmarks for easy navigation, keyboard-friendly links and forms and searchable, selectable text. We recognize the importance of accessibility, and we welcome queries about accessibility for any of our products. If you have a question or an access need, please get in touch with us at accessibilitysupport@springernature.com. Please note that a more accessible version of this eBook is available as ePub.\"}},{\"material\":{\"text\":\"PDF\"},\"summary\":{\"text\":\"No reading system accessibility options actively disabled\"}},{\"material\":{\"text\":\"PDF\"},\"summary\":{\"text\":\"Publisher contact for further accessibility information: accessibilitysupport@springernature.com\"}}],\"catalogingLanguage\":\"eng\",\"citationUrl\":\"https://www.oreilly.com/library/view/-/9798868818202/\",\"contributors\":[{\"firstName\":{\"text\":\"Regine M.\"},\"isPrimary\":true,\"relatorCodes\":[\"aut\"],\"secondName\":{\"text\":\"Gilbert\"}},{\"firstName\":{\"text\":\"Spandita\"},\"isPrimary\":false,\"relatorCodes\":[\"writer of foreword.\"],\"secondName\":{\"text\":\"Sarmah\"}}],\"creator\":\"Regine M. Gilbert\",\"date\":\"2025\",\"doi\":\"10.1007/979-8-8688-1820-2\",\"edition\":\"Second edition\",\"generalFormat\":\"Book\",\"incorrectIsbns\":[\"9798868818196\"],\"isBookReview\":false,\"isNewsArticle\":false,\"isbns\":[\"9798868818202\"],\"language\":\"eng\",\"machineReadableDate\":\"2025\",\"oclcNumber\":\"1548304168\",\"peerReviewed\":\"N\",\"publicationPlace\":\"New York, NY\",\"publisher\":\"Apress\",\"series\":\"Design thinking series\",\"specificFormat\":\"Digital\",\"subjectsText\":[\"Web-based user interfaces\",\"Accessible Web sites for people with disabilities\",\"Assistive computer technology\",\"Interfaces Web\",\"Sites Web accessibles aux personnes handicapées\",\"Technologie informatique adaptée\"],\"summariesText\":[\"Approach digital design with care, curiosity, and the people most often left out. This book invites you to rethink how we create digital systems, products, and tools, not just to meet accessibility requirements, but to shape a more inclusive future. UX design professor and author Regine Gilbert provides a thoughtful, practical, and global perspective on designing with empathy and intention across websites, apps, games, and emerging technologies like AI, VR, and AR. This expanded edition reflects the rapid evolution of the tech landscape. It features up-to-date guidance on the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG 2.2), the European Accessibility Act, and international standards. It also explores the intersection of AI and accessibility, examining both the promises and risks of machine learning, automated tools, and algorithmic bias. You'll learn how to ask better questions, challenge assumptions, and design for real human experiences, especially for those historically excluded. Inclusive Design for a Digital World, Second Edition isn't a checklist or a fix-it manual, it's a collection of reflections, case studies, questions, and examples that help you design with more people in mind from the start. Whether you're working on a subway kiosk, an AI chatbot, a learning app, or a video game, inclusive design is about recognizing who's being left out and doing the work to build systems that allow more people to participate, contribute, and belong. What You Will Learn: Apply WCAG 2.2 and understand how to meet international compliance requirements [if !supportLineBreakNewLine] [endif] Navigate the European Accessibility Act (EAA) and its implications for digital products [if !supportLineBreakNewLine] [endif] Design inclusive experiences for users with visual, motor, auditory, and cognitive disabilities [if !supportLineBreakNewLine] [endif] Identify how AI and machine learning impact accessibility and inclusion--both positively and negatively [if !supportLineBreakNewLine] [endif] Incorporate assistive technologies into your design and testing workflows [if !supportLineBreakNewLine] [endif] Create accessible mobile apps, websites, video games, and immersive experiences like VR and AR [if !supportLineBreakNewLine] [endif] Conduct user research and usability testing with diverse participants [if !supportLineBreakNewLine] [endif] Build inclusive design systems and content architectures from the ground up Who This Book Is For Designers, developers, researchers, product managers, content strategists, educators, and technologists working to embed inclusion into every phase of the digital product lifecycle, with a special emphasis on those exploring the impact of AI on accessibility\"],\"title\":\"Inclusive design for a digital world : designing with accessibility in mind\",\"titleInfo\":{\"text\":\"Inclusive design for a digital world : designing with accessibility in mind\"}}},{\"id\":951150513,\"itemType\":\"BibRecordSummary\",\"title\":\"Accessibility for persons with disabilities and the inclusive future of libraries\",\"creator\":\"John Carlo Bertot\",\"publicationDate\":\"2015\",\"itemRecord\":{\"catalogingLanguage\":\"eng\",\"contributors\":[{\"firstName\":{\"text\":\"John Carlo\"},\"isPrimary\":false,\"relatorCodes\":[\"edt\"],\"secondName\":{\"text\":\"Bertot\"}},{\"contributorNotes\":{\"date\":[\"1974-\"]},\"firstName\":{\"text\":\"Paul T.\"},\"isPrimary\":false,\"relatorCodes\":[\"edt\"],\"secondName\":{\"text\":\"Jaeger\"}},{\"firstName\":{\"text\":\"Brian\"},\"isPrimary\":false,\"relatorCodes\":[\"edt\"],\"secondName\":{\"text\":\"Wentz\"}}],\"creator\":\"John Carlo Bertot\",\"date\":\"2015\",\"generalFormat\":\"Book\",\"incorrectIsbns\":[\"9781785606526\"],\"isBookReview\":false,\"isNewsArticle\":false,\"isbns\":[\"9781785606533\",\"1785606530\"],\"language\":\"eng\",\"machineReadableDate\":\"2015\",\"mergedOclcNumbers\":[\"914573484\",\"914591867\",\"933503971\"],\"oclcNumber\":\"951150513\",\"peerReviewed\":\"N\",\"publicationPlace\":\"United Kingdom\",\"publisher\":\"Emerald Publishing\",\"series\":\"Advances in librarianship\",\"seriesVolumes\":[\"40\"],\"specificFormat\":\"PrintBook\",\"subjectsText\":[\"Libraries and people with disabilities\",\"Libraries Barrier-free design\",\"Bibliothèques et personnes handicapées\",\"Bibliothèques Accessibilité aux personnes handicapées\"],\"summariesText\":[\"All libraries have patrons and staff members with disabilities, making equitable service a priority for these organizations as they provide diverse services to their entire communities. Although rapid technological changes in recent years have offered challenges to libraries, these same technologies provide opportunities to embrace the concept of accessible library services and create innovative new services for patrons with disabilities. Accessibility for Persons with Disabilities and the Inclusive Future of Libraries, edited by Brian Wentz, Paul T. Jaeger, and John Carlo Bertot, focuses on the issues at the intersection of disability, accessibility, inclusion and libraries. The chapters in this volume provide best practices and innovative ideas to share amongst libraries, explore the roles that internet and communication technologies play in the context of inclusive libraries, illuminate the important contributions of libraries in promoting social inclusion of and social justice for people with disabilities, and help libraries to better articulate their contributions in these areas as they engage with disability groups, funders, policymakers, and other parts of their communities\"],\"title\":\"Accessibility for persons with disabilities and the inclusive future of libraries\",\"titleInfo\":{\"text\":\"Accessibility for persons with disabilities and the inclusive future of libraries\"}}},{\"id\":1402812750,\"itemType\":\"BibRecordSummary\",\"title\":\"What every engineer should know about digital accessibility\",\"creator\":\"Sarah Horton\",\"publicationDate\":\"2024\",\"itemRecord\":{\"catalogingLanguage\":\"eng\",\"contributors\":[{\"contributorNotes\":{\"date\":[\"1962-\"]},\"firstName\":{\"text\":\"Sarah\"},\"isPrimary\":true,\"relatorCodes\":[\"aut\"],\"secondName\":{\"text\":\"Horton\"}},{\"contributorNotes\":{\"note\":[\"(Writer on digital accessibility),\"]},\"firstName\":{\"text\":\"David\"},\"isPrimary\":false,\"relatorCodes\":[\"aut\"],\"secondName\":{\"text\":\"Sloan\"}}],\"creator\":\"Sarah Horton\",\"date\":\"2024\",\"edition\":\"First edition\",\"generalFormat\":\"Book\",\"incorrectIsbns\":[\"9781003288060\"],\"isBookReview\":false,\"isNewsArticle\":false,\"isbns\":[\"9781032263854\",\"1032263857\",\"9781032263861\",\"1032263865\"],\"language\":\"eng\",\"machineReadableDate\":\"2024\",\"mergedOclcNumbers\":[\"1402811232\",\"1538104357\"],\"oclcNumber\":\"1402812750\",\"peerReviewed\":\"N\",\"publicationPlace\":\"Boca Raton\",\"publisher\":\"CRC Press, Taylor & Francis Group\",\"series\":\"What every engineer should know\",\"specificFormat\":\"PrintBook\",\"subjectsText\":[\"Software engineering Social aspects\",\"Software engineering Moral and ethical aspects\",\"Computers and people with disabilities\",\"Technology and people with disabilities\",\"Computer software Human factors\",\"Computer software Development\",\"Software architecture Social aspects\",\"User interfaces (Computer systems)\",\"Génie logiciel Aspect social\",\"Ordinateurs et personnes handicapées\",\"Logiciels Facteurs humains\",\"Interfaces utilisateurs (Informatique)\",\"Génie logiciel Aspect moral\",\"Architecture logicielle Aspect social\"],\"summariesText\":[\"\\\"Accessibility is a core quality of digital products to be deliberately addressed throughout the development lifecycle. What Every Engineer Should Know About Digital Accessibility will prepare readers to integrate digital accessibility into their engineering practices. Readers will learn how to accurately frame accessibility as an engineering challenge so they are able to address the correct problems in the correct way. Illustrated with diverse perspectives from accessibility practitioners and advocates, this book describes how people with disabilities use technology, the nature of accessibility barriers in the digital world, and the role of engineers in breaking down those barriers. Accessibility competence for current, emerging, and future technologies is addressed through a combination of guiding principles, core attributes and requirements, and accessibility-informed engineering practices\\\"-- Back cover\"],\"title\":\"What every engineer should know about digital accessibility\",\"titleInfo\":{\"text\":\"What every engineer should know about digital accessibility\"}}},{\"id\":1512666121,\"itemType\":\"BibRecordSummary\",\"title\":\"The digital accessibility handbook for libraries\",\"creator\":\"Carli Spina\",\"publicationDate\":\"2025\",\"itemRecord\":{\"catalogingLanguage\":\"eng\",\"contributors\":[{\"firstName\":{\"text\":\"Carli\"},\"isPrimary\":true,\"relatorCodes\":[\"aut\"],\"secondName\":{\"text\":\"Spina\"}},{\"contributorNotes\":{\"date\":[\"1968-\"]},\"firstName\":{\"text\":\"Rebecca Albrecht\"},\"isPrimary\":false,\"relatorCodes\":[\"aut\"],\"secondName\":{\"text\":\"Oling\"}}],\"creator\":\"Carli Spina\",\"date\":\"2025\",\"generalFormat\":\"Book\",\"incorrectIsbns\":[\"9798892553148\",\"9798892553155\"],\"isBookReview\":false,\"isNewsArticle\":false,\"isbns\":[\"9798892552868\"],\"language\":\"eng\",\"machineReadableDate\":\"2025\",\"mergedOclcNumbers\":[\"1500055298\",\"1558008485\"],\"oclcNumber\":\"1512666121\",\"peerReviewed\":\"N\",\"publicationPlace\":\"Chicago\",\"publisher\":\"ALA Editions in collaboration with Core\",\"specificFormat\":\"PrintBook\",\"subjectsText\":[\"Libraries and people with disabilities United States\",\"Electronic information resources United States\",\"Library resources United States\",\"Computers and people with disabilities United States\",\"Accessible Web sites for people with disabilities\",\"Assistive computer technology\",\"Universal design\",\"Bibliothèques et personnes handicapées États-Unis\",\"Sources d'information électroniques États-Unis\",\"Fonds documentaires États-Unis\",\"Ordinateurs et personnes handicapées États-Unis\",\"Sites Web accessibles aux personnes handicapées\",\"Technologie informatique adaptée\",\"Conception universelle\",\"Libraries and people with disabilities\",\"Electronic information resources\",\"Library resources\",\"Computers and people with disabilities\",\"Instructional and educational works\",\"Matériel d'éducation et de formation\"],\"summariesText\":[\"\\\"In this book, authors dive into digital accessibility in libraries, starting with background information on understanding what is meant by disability and the obligations libraries have to support disabled users\\\"-- Provided by publisher\"],\"title\":\"The digital accessibility handbook for libraries\",\"titleInfo\":{\"text\":\"The digital accessibility handbook for libraries\"}}},{\"id\":1417759218,\"itemType\":\"BibRecordSummary\",\"title\":\"Making the library accessible for all : a practical guide for librarians\",\"creator\":\"Jane Vincent\",\"publicationDate\":\"2024\",\"itemRecord\":{\"catalogingLanguage\":\"eng\",\"contributors\":[{\"firstName\":{\"text\":\"Jane\"},\"isPrimary\":true,\"relatorCodes\":[\"aut\"],\"secondName\":{\"text\":\"Vincent\"}}],\"creator\":\"Jane Vincent\",\"date\":\"2024\",\"edition\":\"Second edition\",\"generalFormat\":\"Book\",\"incorrectIsbns\":[\"9781538176825\"],\"isBookReview\":false,\"isNewsArticle\":false,\"isbns\":[\"9781538176818\",\"1538176815\"],\"language\":\"eng\",\"machineReadableDate\":\"2024\",\"mergedOclcNumbers\":[\"1411030698\",\"1463334639\"],\"oclcNumber\":\"1417759218\",\"peerReviewed\":\"N\",\"publicationPlace\":\"Lanham, Maryland\",\"publisher\":\"Rowman & Littlefield, an imprint of The Rowman & Littlefield Publishing Group, Inc.\",\"series\":\"Practical guides for librarians\",\"seriesVolumes\":[\"no. 81\"],\"specificFormat\":\"PrintBook\",\"subjectsText\":[\"Libraries and people with disabilities\",\"Libraries and people with disabilities United States\",\"Self-help devices for people with disabilities\",\"Assistive computer technology\",\"Bibliothèques et personnes handicapées\",\"Bibliothèques et personnes handicapées États-Unis\",\"Aides fonctionnelles (Médecine physique)\",\"Technologie informatique adaptée\",\"LANGUAGE ARTS & DISCIPLINES / Communication Studies\",\"United States\"],\"summariesText\":[\"\\\"Making the Library Accessible for All is a single-source guide that librarians can refer to when planning, remediating, or evaluating ways to ensure disabled patrons and employees will have successful library experiences. It covers accessibility of communication, hard copy and electronic materials, architecture, trainings and events, technology access, website standards, and a range of related topics\\\"-- Provided by publisher\"],\"title\":\"Making the library accessible for all : a practical guide for librarians\",\"titleInfo\":{\"text\":\"Making the library accessible for all : a practical guide for librarians\"}}},{\"id\":1419271880,\"itemType\":\"BibRecordSummary\",\"title\":\"Web accessibility cookbook : creating inclusive experiences\",\"creator\":\"Manuel Matuzović\",\"publicationDate\":\"2024\",\"itemRecord\":{\"catalogingLanguage\":\"eng\",\"citationUrl\":\"https://www.oreilly.com/library/view/-/9781098145590/\",\"contributors\":[{\"firstName\":{\"text\":\"Manuel\"},\"isPrimary\":true,\"relatorCodes\":[\"aut\"],\"secondName\":{\"text\":\"Matuzović\"}}],\"creator\":\"Manuel Matuzović\",\"date\":\"2024\",\"edition\":\"First edition\",\"generalFormat\":\"Book\",\"incorrectIsbns\":[\"9781098145606\",\"1098145607\"],\"isBookReview\":false,\"isNewsArticle\":false,\"isbns\":[\"9781098145569\",\"1098145569\",\"9781098145576\",\"1098145577\"],\"language\":\"eng\",\"machineReadableDate\":\"2024\",\"mergedOclcNumbers\":[\"1440030078\",\"1459766151\"],\"oclcNumber\":\"1419271880\",\"peerReviewed\":\"N\",\"publicationPlace\":\"Sebastopol, CA\",\"publisher\":\"O'Reilly Media, Inc.\",\"specificFormat\":\"Digital\",\"subjectsText\":[\"Accessible Web sites for people with disabilities\",\"Computers and people with disabilities\",\"Web site development\",\"Web sites Barrier-free design\",\"Sites Web accessibles aux personnes handicapées\",\"Ordinateurs et personnes handicapées\",\"Sites Web Développement\",\"Sites Web Accessibilité aux personnes handicapées\"],\"summariesText\":[\"\\\"Frontend developers have to consider many things: browser compatibility, usability, performance, scalability, SEO, and other best practices. But the most fundamental aspect of creating websites is one that often falls short: accessibility. Accessibility is the cornerstone of any website, and if a website is inaccessible, users won't be able to interact with it, obtain information, sign up for services, or buy products. The Web Accessibility Cookbook provides you with dozens of recipes to help you avoid these failures. You'll learn how to build common components, such as main navigation, filters, and dialogs, in an accessible manner. Each recipe not only explains how to build things but also why. Author Manuel Matuzovic provides the knowledge you need to create your own accessible components and address your users' varying needs, abilities, and preferences.\\\"-- Provided by publisher\"],\"title\":\"Web accessibility cookbook : creating inclusive experiences\",\"titleInfo\":{\"text\":\"Web accessibility cookbook : creating inclusive experiences\"}}},{\"id\":1431047837,\"itemType\":\"BibRecordSummary\",\"title\":\"Practical web accessibility : a comprehensive guide to digital inclusion\",\"creator\":\"Ashley Firth\",\"publicationDate\":\"2024\",\"itemRecord\":{\"catalogingLanguage\":\"eng\",\"citationUrl\":\"https://www.oreilly.com/library/view/-/9798868801525/\",\"contributors\":[{\"firstName\":{\"text\":\"Ashley\"},\"isPrimary\":true,\"relatorCodes\":[\"aut\"],\"secondName\":{\"text\":\"Firth\"}}],\"creator\":\"Ashley Firth\",\"date\":\"2024\",\"doi\":\"10.1007/979-8-8688-0152-5\",\"edition\":\"2nd ed\",\"generalFormat\":\"Book\",\"incorrectIsbns\":[\"9798868801518\"],\"isBookReview\":false,\"isNewsArticle\":false,\"isbns\":[\"9798868801525\"],\"language\":\"eng\",\"machineReadableDate\":\"2024\",\"mergedOclcNumbers\":[\"1430685889\",\"1430755537\",\"1435492667\",\"1586932715\"],\"oclcNumber\":\"1431047837\",\"peerReviewed\":\"N\",\"publicationPlace\":\"London, UK\",\"publisher\":\"Apress\",\"series\":\"ITpro collection\",\"specificFormat\":\"Digital\",\"subjectsText\":[\"Accessible Web sites for people with disabilities\",\"Web sites Design\",\"World Wide Web Access control\",\"World Wide Web Social aspects\",\"Computers and people with disabilities\",\"Assistive computer technology\",\"Sites Web accessibles aux personnes handicapées\",\"Sites Web Conception\",\"Web Accès Contrôle\",\"Web Aspect social\",\"Ordinateurs et personnes handicapées\",\"Technologie informatique adaptée\"],\"summariesText\":[\"Everyone deserves to use the Internet. An estimated 1.3 billion people experience significant disability. That's 16percent of the world's population, or one in six of us. At the same time, over 96 percent of the one million most popular websites have an accessibility issue. Add to this the massive rise in legal cases around sites not being accessible, including Beyonce, Disney, and Netflix, and you have an important topic that more and more people are starting to engage with. In this updated and revamped second edition of the Amazon technology chart-topping Practical Web Accessibility, you'll be guided through a broad range of disabilities and access needs. You'll understand the ways these users typically engage with the web, the barriers they often face, and practical advice on how your websites and content can be compliant, but more than that, inclusive and enjoyable to use. There's also a new chapter on \\\"Outsourcing Accessibility,\\\" exploring third party \\\"bolt-on\\\" tools, \\\"build your own website\\\" platforms like Wix, and popular design systems. You'll explore whether they're helpful or detrimental in the fight to make the web more accessible.Throughout this book you'll learn to test for, spot, and fix web accessibility issues for a wide range of physical and mental impairments. Featuring content from the latest compliance frameworks, including the newly released WCAG 2.2 and exploratory concepts in WCAG 3, you'll see how to go beyond the basic requirements in order to help your users. You'll also learn that an accessible approach won't just help people with disabilities, it will improve your website for everyone. This book comes complete with practical examples you can use in your own sites, along with a brand-new approach to auditing and improving a website's accessibility, and a team's approach to it, based on tools created by the author and refined over years as a consultant -- The FAIR framework and ACCESS checklist. With these tools, you can set up processes for yourself and your team that will drastically improve the accessibility of your sites and, importantly, keep them that way in the future. Suitable for those of any profession or experience level, Practical Web Accessibility gives you all the information you need to ensure that your sites are truly accessible for the modern, inclusive web. If you would like to learn about web accessibility in a clear and actionable way, this book is for you. What You Will Learn A greater understanding of a vast range of disabilities that have online access needs, and the issues they typically face accessing content online. Ways to apply the practical steps required to cater for those needs. How to take your sites, and colleagues, on a journey from being inaccessible to accessible. The importance of accessibility in your designs, code, content, and more. The best ways to test and improve your sites, so you can be compliant, and truly accessible. Who This Book Is For Anyone, regardless of what they do, who wants to learn how to make websites and their content more accessible for those with disabilities. In the world of web, the book has been used by front and backend developers, designers, product and project managers, team and business leaders\"],\"title\":\"Practical web accessibility : a comprehensive guide to digital inclusion\",\"titleInfo\":{\"text\":\"Practical web accessibility : a comprehensive guide to digital inclusion\"}}}]},\"coverArtUrl\":\"https://coverart.oclc.org/ImageWebSvc/oclc\",\"surveymonkeyUrl\":\"https://widget.surveymonkey.com/collect/website/js/tRaiETqnLgj758hTBazgdytE7DtVoTDIOUxEqHANP_2BrRqDRGA3tu_2F5zYA_2FZ3MGN3.js\",\"surveymonkeyToggle\":\"OFF\",\"surveymonkeyHomePageToggle\":\"OFF\",\"displayTemporaryWelcomePage\":\"OFF\",\"mobileBannerToggle\":\"ON\",\"mobileBannerUsToggle\":\"ON\",\"mobileBannerUserMaxRange\":\"1\",\"mobileBannerRandomNumberTesting\":\"1\",\"newRelicBrowserMonitoringToggle\":\"ON\",\"insightsToggle\":\"ON\",\"savedSearchToggle\":\"ON\",\"oclcEnv\":\"PROD\",\"newRelicLicenseKey\":\"NRJS-aaea7133c777fa72dfd\",\"messages\":{\"components.authentication.EmailSigninForm.1094578291\":\"This is a required field\",\"components.authentication.EmailSigninForm.1152665477\":\"Sign in as an institutional user\",\"components.authentication.EmailSigninForm.1479782176\":\"Enter a valid email address\",\"components.authentication.EmailSigninForm.1766832403\":\"Email address\",\"components.authentication.EmailSigninForm.2094698441\":\"Email address not found\",\"components.authentication.EmailSigninForm.2369435044\":\"Required field\",\"components.authentication.EmailSigninForm.359529510\":\"Create a new account\",\"components.authentication.EmailSigninForm.3640052215\":\"Continue\",\"components.authentication.EmailSigninForm.91912734\":\"Unable to process your request. Please try again.\",\"components.authentication.SymbolSigninForm.1346123715\":\"Enter OCLC Symbol\",\"components.authentication.SymbolSigninForm.156130639\":\"Link to look up OCLC Symbols\",\"components.authentication.SymbolSigninForm.1862721931\":\"Need help finding your OCLC symbol?\